{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018sazvor23EMr3ePgSa8ikH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t### class ContactShadow\n2\t\n3\tClassic hard-edged blob shadow that sits on the ground under a character.\n4\tDrawn as a TSL disc (step on distance from center) so it quantizes into a crisp\n5\tpixel ellipse in pixel mode. Position it with `place()` each frame.\n6\t\n7\t- `new ContactShadow(radius = 0.45)`\n8\t- `readonly radius: number`\n9\t- `place(x: number, groundY: number, z: number, height: number): void`\n10\t\n11\t### flicker()\n12\t### glowMaterial()\n13\t\n14\t```ts\n15\tfunction glowMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation): MeshBasicNodeMaterial\n16\t```\n17\t\n18\tUnlit, full-bright material for a colour (flames, eyes, screens, crystal cores), shared and\n19\tcached per colour like `toonMaterial` (`userData.shared`; disposing it drops it from the\n20\tcache). Its vertices snap with the toon materials' under the `ps1` filter, so a glowing part\n21\tstays on its model.\n22\t\n23\t### LIGHT_POOL_SIZES\n24\t### interface LightHandle\n25\t\n26\tA light request. Change it freely; the pool decides whether it currently owns a real light.\n27\t\n28\t- `readonly id: number`\n29\t- `readonly position: Vector3`: World position (mutable; ignored while following).\n30\t- `readonly color: Color`: Colour (mutable).\n31\t- `intensity: number`\n32\t- `radius: number`\n33\t- `decay: number`\n34\t- `flicker: FlickerPreset`\n35\t- `priority: number`\n36\t- `follow: Object3D | null`\n37\t- `readonly offset: Vector3`\n38\t- `name: string`\n39\t- `lifetime: number`: Seconds left before auto-release (Infinity = until `release()`).\n40\t- `update(options: LightRequestOptions): this`: Set several fields at once.\n41\t- `release(): void`: Fade out and give the light back. Safe to call twice.\n42\t- `readonly alive: boolean`\n43\t- `readonly lit: boolean`: Whether it holds one of the pool's real lights right now.\n44\t- `readonly level: number`: 0..1: how much of it is shown (fades).\n45\t\n46\t### interface LightRequestOptions\n47\t\n48\t- `position?: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number]`: World position (copied). Ignored while `follow` is set (then it is `follow` + `offset`).\n49\t- `follow?: Object3D | null`: Follow an object's world position every frame (a projectile, a monster, the hero).\n50\t- `offset?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Offset from `follow` (world axes).\n51\t- `color?: ColorRepresentation`\n52\t- `intensity?: number`: Point light intensity at full strength (before flicker and fades). Default 4.\n53\t- `radius?: number`: Reach in metres (PointLight.distance: light is 0 beyond it). Default 6.\n54\t- `decay?: number`: Distance falloff exponent (PointLight.decay; a uniform, free to change). Default 1.2.\n55\t- `flicker?: FlickerPreset`\n56\t- `priority?: number`: Importance multiplier: the hero's light 4, a loot beam 2, a torch 1 (default).\n57\t- `fadeIn?: number`: Fade times in seconds (defaults 0.25 in, 0.2 out).\n58\t- `fadeOut?: number`\n59\t- `lifetime?: number`: Release automatically after this many seconds (spell flashes, explosions).\n60\t- `name?: string`: Optional label for debugging (`pool.describe()`).\n61\t\n62\t### interface MergeOptions\n63\t### pixelTexture()\n64\t\n65\t```ts\n66\tfunction pixelTexture(texture: T): T\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\tMake a texture pixel-art friendly: nearest-neighbor sampling, no mipmaps. Returns it.\n70\t\n71\t### TOON_BANDS\n72\t### toonMaterial()\n73\t\n74\t```ts\n75\tfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\n76\t```\n77\t\n78\tShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\n79\tvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\n80\t(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\n81\t`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\n82\tdisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\n83\t\n84\t### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n85\t\n86\t- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\n87\t- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\n88\t- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\n89\t- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\n90\t\n91\t### interface ClipDef\n92\t\n93\t- `name: string`\n94\t- `frames: number`: Length in frames at 30 fps.\n95\t- `loop?: boolean`\n96\t- `keys: readonly Key[]`\n97\t- `layers?: readonly Layer[]`\n98\t- `feet?: readonly FeetKey[]`: Feet track: foot goals interpolated between its own keys and solved with IK every frame, overriding the keyed leg rotations. Use it whenever feet touch the floor through a transition (kneel → stand, sit → lie) so they roll instead of sinking.\n99\t- `speed?: number`: Ground speed (m/s) the clip is authored for at playback rate 1. Locomotion clips set this; metrics then measure foot sliding against it and the runtime can scale playback.\n100\t- `stance?: number`: Gait cycles (gaitClip): the share of the cycle each foot is planted. The right heel strikes at phase 0, the left at 0.5, so the right foot is mid-stance at `stance / 2`.\n101\t- `reach?: number`: Gaits: how far ahead of the hips (m) the middle of the stance is (feet touch down `reach` + half a stance's ground ahead).\n102\t- `grounded?: boolean`: Grounded clip: soles should rest on y = 0 (metrics flag floating / penetration).\n103\t- `fast?: boolean`: Intentionally snappy (flips, punches, launches): skip the angular-speed warning.\n104\t- `notes?: string`\n105\t\n106\t### interface ClipReport\n107\t\n108\tObjective checks for a clip, computed by actually posing the rig (no renderer). These\n109\tare the numbers an agent can't eyeball: foot sliding, ground contact, loop seams,\n110\tvelocity spikes, joint limits. Thresholds are deliberately forgiving; `problems` are\n111\treal defects, `warnings` are worth a look.\n112\t\n113\t- `name: string`\n114\t- `frames: number`\n115\t- `loop: boolean`\n116\t- `speed: number | null`\n117\t- `minSoleY: number`: Lowest sole point over the clip (m) and the frame it happens. Negative = through the floor.\n118\t- `minSoleFrame: number`\n119\t- `minBodyY: number`: Lowest point of any other body part (knees, hands, head...), where and when.\n120\t- `minBodyMesh: string`\n121\t- `minBodyFrame: number`\n122\t- `floatingFrames: number`: Frames (of grounded clips) where neither sole is within 5 cm of the floor.\n123\t- `footSlide: number`: Mean horizontal slip of the planted foot, m/s (0 = perfectly planted).\n124\t- `loopSeam: number`: Largest joint-angle jump between the last and first frame of a loop, degrees.\n125\t- `maxAngularSpeed: { joint: string; degPerSec: number; frame: number }`: Fastest joint rotation, degrees per second, and where.\n126\t- `limitViolations: { joint: string; axis: 'x' | 'y' | 'z'; frame: number; value: number; range: [number, number] }[]`\n127\t- `pelvisY: [number, number]`: Pelvis height range (m) — how much the body bobs.\n128\t- `problems: string[]`\n129\t- `warnings: string[]`\n130\t\n131\t### compileClip()\n132\t\n133\t```ts\n134\tfunction compileClip(def: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec, rest: RestPose): AnimationClip\n135\t```\n136\t\n137\tBake a ClipDef into a three.js AnimationClip (quaternion + position + scale tracks,\n138\tsampled at 60 Hz so easing and per-axis Euler interpolation — including 360° flips —\n139\tsurvive exactly).\n140\t\n141\t### compileClips()\n142\t\n143\t```ts\n144\tfunction compileClips(defs: readonly ClipDef[], rig: RigSpec, model: Object3D): AnimationClip[]\n145\t```\n146\t\n147\t### interface Foot\n148\t\n149\t- `readonly at: Vec3`: World position of the foot now.\n150\t- `t: number`: Stepping: 0 → 1 through the step; -1 planted.\n151\t- `readonly from: Vec3`\n152\t- `readonly to: Vec3`\n153\t\n154\t### interface FootGoal\n155\t\n156\tFoot-placement IK: say where a foot should be, get the hip/knee/ankle rotations.\n157\t\n158\tAuthors write the body (pelvis height, lean, arms...) and then pin the feet:\n159\t\n160\t  placeFeet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Torso: [20, 0, 0] }, rig, {\n161\t    R: { z: 0.15 },                             // right foot flat, 15 cm ahead\n162\t    L: { z: -0.2, pitch: 30, pivot: 'ball' },   // left heel raised on its toes\n163\t  })\n164\t\n165\tCoordinates are the character's ground frame: y up from the floor, z forward. The solve\n166\tis planar (legs bend about X, knees forward); lateral offsets are ignored. It accounts\n167\tfor the root's position, rotation and squash, so a squashed or leaning body still\n168\tkeeps its feet exactly where they were asked…\n169\t\n170\t- `z: number`: Forward position of the ankle (m) when the foot is flat.\n171\t- `x?: number`: Sideways position (m, + = the character's left). Default: under the hip at rest. Only matters when the root is turned (e.g. a pivot on one foot); the solve itself stays in the leg's plane.\n172\t- `y?: number`: Height of the sole above the floor (m). 0 = standing on it.\n173\t- `pitch?: number`: Sole pitch in degrees: + = toes down / heel raised, − = toes up.\n174\t- `pivot?: 'heel' | 'ball' | 'ankle'`: Point that stays at (z, y) while pitching: heel (heel strike), toe tip (tiptoe, toe-off) or ankle.\n175\t- `follow?: number`: 0..1: let the foot hang from the shin instead of holding its world pitch (swinging feet, dangling in the air). 1 = foot at `relax` degrees relative to the shin.\n176\t- `relax?: number`: Foot angle relative to the shin when following (default 15 = toes slightly down).\n177\t\n178\t### gaitClip()\n179\t\n180\t```ts\n181\tfunction gaitClip(rig: RigSpec, g: GaitSpec): ClipDef\n182\t```\n183\t\n184\t### gaitPartners()\n185\t### class SpringChain\n186\t\n187\tA chain of points hanging off a moving root. Call `update(dt, root, basis)` every frame\n188\twith the root's world position and its orientation (three columns: right, up, forward),\n189\tthen read `points` (root first).\n190\t\n191\t- `new SpringChain(o: SpringChainOptions)`\n192\t- `readonly points: Vec3[]`\n193\t- `o: Required<SpringChainOptions>`\n194\t- `reset(root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`: Put the chain straight out in its rest pose (no swing).\n195\t- `update(dt: number, root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`\n196\t- `swing(basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): number`: How far the tip is from where the rest pose puts it (m): how much it is swinging.\n197\t\n198\t### interface SpringChainOptions\n199\t\n200\t- `segments: number`: Points after the root (≥ 1).\n201\t- `length: number`: Length of each segment (m).\n202\t- `rest?: Vec3`: Rest direction from the root in the root's own space (normalised; default straight back, −Z).\n203\t- `stiffness?: number`: Pull toward the rest pose per second (0 floppy … 30 stiff). Default 10.\n204\t- `keep?: number`: Velocity kept per 1/60 s (0..1). Default 0.94.\n205\t- `gravity?: number`: Gravity on the chain (m/s²). Default 6 (lighter than real: tails hold up a bit).\n206\t\n207\t### class Squash\n208\t\n209\tSquash and stretch as a damped spring on `value` (0 = rest, + stretched, − squashed).\n210\t`scale()` turns it into a volume-preserving pair: `const [h, v] = squash.scale();\n211\tmesh.scale.set(h, v, h)`.\n212\t\n213\t- `value: number`\n214\t- `velocity: number`\n215\t- `stiffness: number`: Spring stiffness and damping (a critically damped spring has damping = 2√stiffness).\n216\t- `damping: number`\n217\t- `amount: number`: 0 turns it off; 2.5 is rubbery.\n218\t- `kick(v: number): void`: Add a kick: negative squashes (a landing), positive stretches (a jump).\n219\t- `set(v: number): void`: Set the shape directly (a held squash).\n220\t- `update(dt: number): void`\n221\t- `scale(out: [number, number] = [1, 1]): [number, number]`: [horizontal, vertical] scale: y = 1 + s, xz = 1 / √(1 + s), so the volume stays put.\n222\t\n223\t### twoBoneIK()\n224\t\n225\t```ts\n226\tfunction twoBoneIK(root: Vec3, target: Vec3, a: number, b: number, pole: Vec3, out: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0]): Vec3\n227\t```\n228\t\n229\tWhere the middle joint of a two-bone limb goes (a knee, an elbow) so the end reaches\n230\t`target` from `root` with bones `a` and `b` long, bending toward `pole` (a point the knee\n231\tpoints at). Analytic (the law of cosines), no iterations; a target out of reach straightens\n232\tthe limb toward it, one too close folds it as far as it goes. Returns the joint, into `out`.\n233\t\n234\t### validateClip()\n235\t\n236\t```ts\n237\tfunction validateClip(clip: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec): string[]\n238\t```\n239\t\n240\tProblems with a clip definition itself (unknown joints, bad key order, loop mismatch).\n241\t### applySky()\n242\t\n243\t```ts\n244\tfunction applySky(engine: Pick<Engine, 'sun' | 'ambient' | 'scene' | 'setSunDirection'>, s: SkyState): void\n245\t```\n246\t\n247\tPut a sky on the engine: sun direction, colour and strength, ambient light, background.\n248\t\n249\t### bayer4()\n250\t\n251\t```ts\n252\tfunction bayer4(): any\n253\t```\n254\t\n255\tA 4 x 4 ordered dither threshold per art pixel (0..1): keep a pixel where it is below its opacity.\n256\t### class Boids\n257\t\n258\t- `new Boids(count: number, o: BoidOptions = {})`\n259\t- `readonly count: number`\n260\t- `readonly pos: Float32Array`\n261\t- `readonly vel: Float32Array`\n262\t- `o: Required<Omit<BoidOptions, 'bounds' | 'seed'>> & { bounds: BoidOptions['bounds'] }`\n263\t- `seek: Vec3 | null`: A point everyone is drawn toward (null: none).\n264\t- `seekWeight: number`\n265\t- `flee: { at: Vec3; radius: number } | null`: A threat to scatter from.\n266\t- `fleeWeight: number`\n267\t- `obstacles: { x: number; y: number; z: number; r: number }[]`: Spheres to steer around (x, y, z, r).\n268\t- `spacing(): number`: Average distance to the nearest neighbour (tests, tools).\n269\t- `order(): { speed: number; alignment: number }`: Average speed and how lined up the headings are (0 random, 1 all the same way).\n270\t- `step(dt: number): void`\n271\t\n272\t### interface Branch\n273\t\n274\t- `from: V3`\n275\t### class Decals\n276\t\n277\t- `new Decals(scene: Scene, o: { capacity?: number } = {})`\n278\t- `readonly meshes: Map<\"ring\" | \"crack\" | \"footprint\" | \"scorch\" | \"splat\", InstancedMesh<BufferGeometry<NormalBufferAttributes, BufferGeometryEventMap>, Material<...> | Material…`\n279\t- `readonly o: { capacity?: number }`\n280\t- `add(shape: DecalShape, at: Vector3Like, normal: Vector3Like, o: DecalOptions = {}): number`: Lay a mark at `at` on a surface facing `normal`. Returns its index in that shape's pool.\n281\t- `count(shape?: DecalShape): number`: Marks alive (per shape or all).\n282\t- `update(dt: number): void`: Per frame: age the marks; old ones dither away over a second.\n283\t- `clear(): void`: Remove every mark (the meshes stay for reuse).\n284\t- `dispose(): void`\n285\t\n286\t### type DecalShape\n287\t\n288\t```ts\n289\ttype DecalShape = (typeof DECAL_SHAPES)[number]\n290\t```\n291\t\n292\t### decodeState()\n293\t\n294\t```ts\n295\tfunction decodeState(v: unknown): unknown\n296\t```\n297\t\n298\t`encodeState` undone: a deep copy with the marked numbers (and the game's own `@` strings) back.\n299\t\n300\t### drawSheet()\n301\t### groundFog()\n302\t\n303\t```ts\n304\tfunction groundFog(o: { color?: number; top?: number; amount?: number; near?: number; far?: number } = {}): { node: Node; color: UniformNode<\"color\", Color>; amount: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; top: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; }\n305\t```\n306\t\n307\tFog for `scene.fogNode` with live settings (uniforms: changing them never recompiles):\n308\tground mist that thickens below `top` (m) and a haze that grows with distance from the\n309\tcamera, both up to `amount` (0..1), in `color` (match the sky).\n310\t\n311\t  const mist = groundFog({ color: s.sky, top: 1.5 });\n312\t  (scene as { fogNode: unknown }).fogNode = mist.node;\n313\t  mist.amount.value = 0.8; mist.color.value.setHex(s.sky);\n314\t### class Mirror\n315\t\n316\t- `new Mirror(o: MirrorOptions = {})`\n317\t- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n318\t- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n319\t- `enabled: boolean`: False: the glass shows plain glass and nothing is rendered for it.\n320\t- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n321\t- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene, camera: Camera, width: number, height: number): boolean`: Reflect `camera` in the glass and draw `scene` from there into the texture (sized `width` x `height`, the art resolution). Skipped when the camera is behind the glass.\n322\t- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`), from its camera, at its art size. Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs (nothing is drawn).\n323\t- `dispose(): void`\n324\t\n325\t### interface MirrorOptions\n326\t\n327\t- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Width and height of the glass (m). Default [4, 2].\n328\t- `tint?: number`: A colour the reflection leans toward, and how much (0..1). Default a faint blue, 0.15.\n329\t- `tintAmount?: number`\n330\t\n331\t### class NavGrid\n332\t\n333\t- `new NavGrid(width: number, height: number, o: NavGridOptions = {})`\n334\t- `static fromRows(rows: readonly string[], o: NavGridOptions & { blocked?: string } = {}): NavGrid`: From an ASCII map: `blocked` characters are closed, everything else open. Default '# ': walls and pits (a ' ' has no floor in RoomKit's maps); past the end of a short row is a wall.\n335\t- `readonly width: number`\n336\t- `readonly height: number`\n337\t- `readonly cell: number`\n338\t- `readonly ox: number`: World x, z of cell (0, 0)'s corner.\n339\t- `readonly oz: number`\n340\t- `readonly open: Uint8Array`: 1 = walkable.\n341\t- `version: number`: Bumped by `setOpen`: flow fields rebuild.\n342\t- `flowBuilds: number`: How many times a flow field was built (tools: should be one per target cell change).\n343\t- `col(x: number): number`\n344\t- `row(z: number): number`\n345\t- `centerX(col: number): number`: World x, z of a cell's centre.\n346\t- `centerZ(row: number): number`\n347\t- `isOpen(col: number, row: number): boolean`\n348\t- `walkable(x: number, z: number): boolean`: Is the world point on a walkable cell?\n349\t- `setOpen(col: number, row: number, open: boolean): void`\n350\t- `path(from: readonly [number, number, number], to: readonly [number, number, number]): [number, number, number][] | null`: Shortest path between two world points (x, z used; y kept from `from`): A* over cells, no corner cutting, then smoothed so it only turns where a wall is in the way. Null when there is no way. The first point is `from`, the last `to` (s\n351\t- `smooth(pts: [number, number, number][]): [number, number, number][]`: Drop every point the path can skip in a straight line.\n352\t- `lineOfSight(ax: number, az: number, bx: number, bz: number, radius = 0): boolean`: Can you see (or walk straight) from a to b? Walks the cells under the segment (a DDA); `radius` > 0 also tests two lines offset sideways (a body that wide fits).\n353\t- `castWall(ax: number, az: number, dx: number, dz: number, max: number): number`: Distance from a along a direction to the first closed cell (at most `max`): the same cell walk as `lineOfSight`, so a vision cone drawn with it shows exactly what a guard can see.\n354\t- `flowTo(x: number, z: number): boolean`: A flow field toward the world point (x, z): the walking distance from every cell to it. Rebuilt only when the target changes cell or the grid changed (`version`). Returns whether it was rebuilt.\n355\t- `flowDistance(x: number, z: number): number`: Walking distance to the flow target from a world point (Infinity: no way).\n356\t- `flowDirection(x: number, z: number, out: [number, number]): boolean`: Which way to go from (x, z) toward the flow target: the unit direction to the lowest-distance neighbour (into `out` [x, z]). Returns false at the target or with no way.\n357\t\n358\t### interface NavGridOptions\n359\t\n360\tNavigation on a grid: which cells can be walked, the shortest path between two points\n361\t(A*, 8-connected, no corner cutting, smoothed by line of sight), a flow field toward one\n362\ttarget (one Dijkstra fill, then any number of agents read a direction per cell for free),\n363\tand line-of-sight tests (vision cones, stealth). Pure and allocation-light; unit-tested.\n364\t\n365\t  const nav = NavGrid.fromRows(['#########', '#...#...#', '#.#...#.#', '#########'], { cell: 1, origin: [-4.5, 0, -2] });\n366\t  const path = nav.path([-3, 0, -1], [3, 0, -1]);       // world points, corners only\n367\t  nav.flowTo(hero.x, hero.z);                            // once when the target changes cell\n368\t  nav.flowDirection(x, z, out);…\n369\t\n370\t- `cell?: number`: Metres per cell. Default 1.\n371\t- `origin?: readonly [number, number, number]`: World x, z of the top-left cell's corner (column 0, row 0). Default: centred on the origin.\n372\t\n373\t### interface Noise\n374\t\n375\t- `readonly seed: number`\n376\t### class Precipitation\n377\t\n378\t- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n379\t- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n380\t- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n381\t- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n382\t- `get intensity: number`: Share of the drops falling (0..1).\n383\t- `get speed: number`: Fall speed (m/s).\n384\t- `update(dt: number, center: Vector3): void`: Per frame (game time): advance the fall and follow `center`.\n385\t- `splashes(dt: number): number`: How many drops hit the ground in `dt` seconds at this intensity (for splash particles, ripples).\n386\t- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n387\t\n388\t### type PrecipitationKind\n389\t\n390\t```ts\n391\ttype PrecipitationKind = 'rain' | 'snow'\n392\t```\n393\t\n394\t### interface PrecipitationOptions\n395\t\n396\t- `kind: PrecipitationKind`\n397\t- `count: number`: Most drops at once (the instance count).\n398\t- `area?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Width, height and depth of the air the drops fall through, around the centre.\n399\t- `color?: number`: Drop colour (hex).\n400\t- `speed?: number`: Fall speed (m/s). Rain 16, snow 1.4.\n401\t\n402\t### interface Recording\n403\t\n404\t- `readonly format: 1`\n405\t- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that recorded it (a different one may not replay the same).\n406\t- `readonly game: string`: The game's name when it was recorded.\n407\t### class RenderView\n408\t\n409\t- `new RenderView(o: RenderViewOptions = {})`\n410\t- `static screen(object: Object3D): void`: Put `object` (and its children) on the screens' layer.\n411\t- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n412\t- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n413\t- `every: number`: Render every nth frame.\n414\t- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n415\t- `enabled: boolean`\n416\t- `get texture: Texture`\n417\t- `setSize(w: number, h: number): void`: Resize the texture (the camera's aspect follows).\n418\t- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene): boolean`: Draw `scene` from the view's camera into its texture, if this is one of its frames. True if it drew.\n419\t- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`). Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs.\n420\t- `screenMaterial(): MeshBasicNodeMaterial`: An unlit material showing the view (a new one each call: tint it as you like).\n421\t- `dispose(): void`\n422\t\n423\t### interface RenderViewOptions\n424\t\n425\t- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Texture size in pixels (default [160, 90]).\n426\t- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view, degrees (default 60).\n427\t- `near?: number`\n428\t- `far?: number`\n429\t- `every?: number`: Render every nth frame (default 1): a slow refresh costs less.\n430\t\n431\t### class Rng\n432\t\n433\tSeeded randomness. Everything random in a game comes from an `Rng`, so the same seed always\n434\tgives the same result (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1). Each level gets one, `ctx.random`,\n435\tseeded from the engine's seed and the game's name; fork it by purpose so streams stay\n436\tindependent of how many numbers each one drew:\n437\t\n438\t  const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\n439\t  const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\n440\t\n441\tNever use Math.random in game or engine code (the lint refuses it).\n442\t\n443\t- `new Rng(seed: number | string)`\n444\t- `get state: number`: The generator's whole state: save it, and set it back to draw the same numbers again.\n445\t- `next(): number`: Uniform in [0, 1). mulberry32.\n446\t- `fork(purpose: string | number): Rng`: A child generator for one purpose; does not advance this one.\n447\t- `range(min: number, max: number): number`: Float in [min, max).\n448\t- `int(min: number, max: number): number`: Integer in [min, max] (inclusive).\n449\t- `chance(p: number): boolean`\n450\t- `pick(items: readonly T[]): T`\n451\t### skyAt()\n452\t\n453\t```ts\n454\tfunction skyAt(hour: number): SkyState\n455\t```\n456\t\n457\tThe sky at `hour` (wraps around 24).\n458\t\n459\t### interface SkyState\n460\t\n461\t- `readonly sunDir: [number, number, number]`: Unit vector toward the sun (or the moon, at night).\n462\t- `readonly sunColor: number`\n463\t- `readonly sunIntensity: number`\n464\t- `readonly ambientColor: number`\n465\t- `readonly ambientIntensity: number`\n466\t- `readonly sky: number`: Background (sky) and fog colour.\n467\t- `readonly night: number`: 0 by day, 1 deep at night: lanterns, stars, windows.\n468\t\n469\t### interface Snapshot\n470\t\n471\t- `readonly format: 1`\n472\t- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that took it (a different one may not restore the same).\n473\t- `readonly game: string`: The game's name: a snapshot restores into the same game.\n474\t- `readonly seed: number`: The engine seed and game time when it was taken.\n475\t- `readonly time: number`\n476\t- `readonly clock: ClockState`\n477\t- `readonly random: number`: `ctx.random`'s state.\n478\t- `readonly physics: PhysicsState`\n479\t### swayObject()\n480\t\n481\t```ts\n482\tfunction swayObject(root: Object3D, wind: WindUniforms, o: SwayOptions): void\n483\t```\n484\t\n485\tMake every mesh under `root` sway (its materials replaced by swaying copies).\n486\t\n487\t### interface SwayOptions\n488\t\n489\t- `height: number`: Height (in the mesh's own units) of its top: the lean is 0 at `base` and full there.\n490\t- `base?: number`: Where the lean starts (the trunk below stays still). Default 0.\n491\t- `amount?: number`: Lean at the top per unit of wind. Default 0.15.\n492\t- `phase?: number`: Its own phase (radians): neighbours don't move in lockstep.\n493\t\n494\t### type Team\n495\t\n496\t```ts\n497\ttype Team = 'enemy' | 'player'\n498\t```\n499\t\n500\t### class Timeline\n501\t\n502\t- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n503\t- `readonly duration: number`\n504\t- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n505\t- `playing: boolean`\n506\t- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n507\t- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n508\t- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n509\t- `play(): void`\n510\t- `pause(): void`\n511\t- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n512\t- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n513\t- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n514\t- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and out). A `cut` key starts a new shot. Null witho…\n515\t- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n516\t- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n517\t\n518\t### interface TimelineLine\n519\t\n520\t- `at: number`\n521\t- `until: number`\n522\t- `text: string`\n523\t- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n524\t\n525\t### interface TimelineOptions\n526\t\n527\t- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n528\t- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n529\t- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n530\t- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n531\t- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n532\t- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n533\t\n534\t### interface TraceRow\n535\t\n536\t- `name: string`\n537\t- `kind: string`\n538\t- `depth: number`\n539\t- `status: Status | null`: This tick's answer, or null if this tick never reached the node.\n540\t### class Tweens\n541\t\n542\tA set of running tweens (the engine keeps one per game: `ctx.tweens`).\n543\t\n544\t- `get count: number`: Tweens still running.\n545\t- `to(target: T, to: Partial<Record<keyof T, number>>, options: TweenOptions = {}): Tween`: Glide `target`'s numeric properties to `to`. A new tween on the same target and property takes over (the old one stops where it is).\n546\t- `value(from: number, to: number, options: TweenOptions, apply: (v: number) => void): Tween`: Tween a plain number from `from` to `to`, calling `apply(v)` every frame.\n547\t- `call(seconds: number, fn: () => void): Tween`: Call `fn` after `seconds` of game time.\n548\t- `cancel(target?: object): void`: Stop every tween on `target` (or everything).\n549\t- `clear(): void`: Stop everything (level unload). Pending `done` promises resolve.\n550\t- `update(dt: number): void`\n551\t\n552\t### interface View\n553\t\n554\t- `readonly container: HTMLElement | null`: The page element the canvas sits in; null headless.\n555\t- `readonly backend: BackendName`\n556\t- `readonly gpuErrors: readonly GpuErrorRecord[]`\n557\t- `readonly recoveries: number`: How many times a lost GPU device was recovered from (0 headless).\n558\t### class WaterSurface\n559\t\n560\t- `new WaterSurface(o: WaterOptions)`\n561\t- `readonly size: readonly [number, number]`\n562\t- `waves: Wave[]`\n563\t- `readonly ripples: RippleField | null`\n564\t- `readonly uOpacity: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n565\t- `readonly uFoamAt: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n566\t- `setWaves(waves: readonly Wave[]): void`: Change the waves (up to MAX_WAVES; the CPU height follows too).\n567\t- `update(time: number, sun?: Vector3): void`: Per frame: the waves' clock (use physics time: floaters read the same), the ripples, the sun.\n568\t- `heightAt(x: number, z: number, t = this.time): number`: World height of the drawn surface at (x, z) (waves and ripples), at the last `update` time or `t`.\n569\t- `covers(x: number, z: number): boolean`: Is (x, z) over this water?\n570\t- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n571\t\n572\t### class Wfc\n573\t\n574\t- `new Wfc(tiles: readonly WfcTile[], width: number, height: number, o: WfcOptions = {})`\n575\t- `readonly tiles: readonly WfcTile[]`\n576\t- `readonly wave: Uint8Array`: Options still open per cell: `wave[cell * tiles + t]` is 1 while tile t is possible.\n577\t- `readonly options: Uint16Array`: How many options each cell has left.\n578\t- `readonly result: Int32Array`: The chosen tile per cell (−1 until it has one option left).\n579\t- `attempt: number`: Starts so far (1 + the contradictions met).\n580\t- `done: boolean`: True once every cell has one tile, false while solving or after giving up.\n581\t- `failed: boolean`\n582\t- `choices: number`: Cells collapsed by choice (the rest followed from propagation).\n583\t- `readonly width: number`\n584\t- `readonly height: number`\n585\t- `restart(): void`: Start again from scratch (each start after the first uses the next seed).\n586\t- `run(): boolean`: Solve to the end (restarting on contradictions). True if every cell has a tile.\n587\t- `step(): boolean`: One collapse: the cell with the least entropy gets one tile, and that is propagated. Returns false when there is nothing left to do (solved, or given up).\n588\t- `entropy(c: number): number`: Shannon entropy of a cell's options, by weight (0 when it has one left).\n589\t\n590\t### interface WfcOptions\n591\t\n592\t- `seed?: number`\n593\t- `border?: string`: The socket every edge on the grid's outside must be (a closed map: '###'). Default: any.\n594\t- `fixed?: Readonly<Record<number, number>>`: Cells set before solving: cell index (x + y × width) → tile index (they may break the border: a way in).\n595\t- `attempts?: number`: Starts allowed before giving up on contradictions (default 30).\n596\t\n597\t### interface WfcTile\n598\t\n599\t- `readonly name: string`\n600\t- `readonly edges: readonly [string, string, string, string]`: North (−z, up the map), east (+x), south (+z), west (−x).\n601\t- `readonly weight?: number`: How often it is chosen, relative to the others (default 1).\n602\t\n603\t### class WindUniforms\n604\t\n605\t- `readonly time: any`\n606\t- `readonly wind: any`\n607\t- `update(time: number, wind: Vector2 | readonly [number, number]): void`: Per frame (game time); `wind` along x and z (its length is the strength).\n608\t\n609\t### woodMaterial()\n610\t\n611\t```ts\n612\tfunction woodMaterial(o: ShaderOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\n613\t```\n614\t\n615\tWood: rings round the y axis, wobbled by noise, light and dark grain, toon-lit.\n616\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4cb4937-9264-42cc-b44d-b76eca04b6e6","uuid":"c6a3460e-9f8b-400c-a6f4-72225dd0d0a3","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:19:21.266Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build-v2--20261105-171818--x10629c-work/a4cb4937-9264-42cc-b44d-b76eca04b6e6/tool-results/bz3n2jx9m.txt","content":"### class ContactShadow\n\nClassic hard-edged blob shadow that sits on the ground under a character.\nDrawn as a TSL disc (step on distance from center) so it quantizes into a crisp\npixel ellipse in pixel mode. Position it with `place()` each frame.\n\n- `new ContactShadow(radius = 0.45)`\n- `readonly radius: number`\n- `place(x: number, groundY: number, z: number, height: number): void`\n\n### flicker()\n### glowMaterial()\n\n```ts\nfunction glowMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation): MeshBasicNodeMaterial\n```\n\nUnlit, full-bright material for a colour (flames, eyes, screens, crystal cores), shared and\ncached per colour like `toonMaterial` (`userData.shared`; disposing it drops it from the\ncache). Its vertices snap with the toon materials' under the `ps1` filter, so a glowing part\nstays on its model.\n\n### LIGHT_POOL_SIZES\n### interface LightHandle\n\nA light request. Change it freely; the pool decides whether it currently owns a real light.\n\n- `readonly id: number`\n- `readonly position: Vector3`: World position (mutable; ignored while following).\n- `readonly color: Color`: Colour (mutable).\n- `intensity: number`\n- `radius: number`\n- `decay: number`\n- `flicker: FlickerPreset`\n- `priority: number`\n- `follow: Object3D | null`\n- `readonly offset: Vector3`\n- `name: string`\n- `lifetime: number`: Seconds left before auto-release (Infinity = until `release()`).\n- `update(options: LightRequestOptions): this`: Set several fields at once.\n- `release(): void`: Fade out and give the light back. Safe to call twice.\n- `readonly alive: boolean`\n- `readonly lit: boolean`: Whether it holds one of the pool's real lights right now.\n- `readonly level: number`: 0..1: how much of it is shown (fades).\n\n### interface LightRequestOptions\n\n- `position?: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number]`: World position (copied). Ignored while `follow` is set (then it is `follow` + `offset`).\n- `follow?: Object3D | null`: Follow an object's world position every frame (a projectile, a monster, the hero).\n- `offset?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Offset from `follow` (world axes).\n- `color?: ColorRepresentation`\n- `intensity?: number`: Point light intensity at full strength (before flicker and fades). Default 4.\n- `radius?: number`: Reach in metres (PointLight.distance: light is 0 beyond it). Default 6.\n- `decay?: number`: Distance falloff exponent (PointLight.decay; a uniform, free to change). Default 1.2.\n- `flicker?: FlickerPreset`\n- `priority?: number`: Importance multiplier: the hero's light 4, a loot beam 2, a torch 1 (default).\n- `fadeIn?: number`: Fade times in seconds (defaults 0.25 in, 0.2 out).\n- `fadeOut?: number`\n- `lifetime?: number`: Release automatically after this many seconds (spell flashes, explosions).\n- `name?: string`: Optional label for debugging (`pool.describe()`).\n\n### interface MergeOptions\n### pixelTexture()\n\n```ts\nfunction pixelTexture(texture: T): T\n```\n\nMake a texture pixel-art friendly: nearest-neighbor sampling, no mipmaps. Returns it.\n\n### TOON_BANDS\n### toonMaterial()\n\n```ts\nfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\n```\n\nShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\nvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\n(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\n`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\ndisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\n\n### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\n\n### interface ClipDef\n\n- `name: string`\n- `frames: number`: Length in frames at 30 fps.\n- `loop?: boolean`\n- `keys: readonly Key[]`\n- `layers?: readonly Layer[]`\n- `feet?: readonly FeetKey[]`: Feet track: foot goals interpolated between its own keys and solved with IK every frame, overriding the keyed leg rotations. Use it whenever feet touch the floor through a transition (kneel → stand, sit → lie) so they roll instead of sinking.\n- `speed?: number`: Ground speed (m/s) the clip is authored for at playback rate 1. Locomotion clips set this; metrics then measure foot sliding against it and the runtime can scale playback.\n- `stance?: number`: Gait cycles (gaitClip): the share of the cycle each foot is planted. The right heel strikes at phase 0, the left at 0.5, so the right foot is mid-stance at `stance / 2`.\n- `reach?: number`: Gaits: how far ahead of the hips (m) the middle of the stance is (feet touch down `reach` + half a stance's ground ahead).\n- `grounded?: boolean`: Grounded clip: soles should rest on y = 0 (metrics flag floating / penetration).\n- `fast?: boolean`: Intentionally snappy (flips, punches, launches): skip the angular-speed warning.\n- `notes?: string`\n\n### interface ClipReport\n\nObjective checks for a clip, computed by actually posing the rig (no renderer). These\nare the numbers an agent can't eyeball: foot sliding, ground contact, loop seams,\nvelocity spikes, joint limits. Thresholds are deliberately forgiving; `problems` are\nreal defects, `warnings` are worth a look.\n\n- `name: string`\n- `frames: number`\n- `loop: boolean`\n- `speed: number | null`\n- `minSoleY: number`: Lowest sole point over the clip (m) and the frame it happens. Negative = through the floor.\n- `minSoleFrame: number`\n- `minBodyY: number`: Lowest point of any other body part (knees, hands, head...), where and when.\n- `minBodyMesh: string`\n- `minBodyFrame: number`\n- `floatingFrames: number`: Frames (of grounded clips) where neither sole is within 5 cm of the floor.\n- `footSlide: number`: Mean horizontal slip of the planted foot, m/s (0 = perfectly planted).\n- `loopSeam: number`: Largest joint-angle jump between the last and first frame of a loop, degrees.\n- `maxAngularSpeed: { joint: string; degPerSec: number; frame: number }`: Fastest joint rotation, degrees per second, and where.\n- `limitViolations: { joint: string; axis: 'x' | 'y' | 'z'; frame: number; value: number; range: [number, number] }[]`\n- `pelvisY: [number, number]`: Pelvis height range (m) — how much the body bobs.\n- `problems: string[]`\n- `warnings: string[]`\n\n### compileClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction compileClip(def: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec, rest: RestPose): AnimationClip\n```\n\nBake a ClipDef into a three.js AnimationClip (quaternion + position + scale tracks,\nsampled at 60 Hz so easing and per-axis Euler interpolation — including 360° flips —\nsurvive exactly).\n\n### compileClips()\n\n```ts\nfunction compileClips(defs: readonly ClipDef[], rig: RigSpec, model: Object3D): AnimationClip[]\n```\n\n### interface Foot\n\n- `readonly at: Vec3`: World position of the foot now.\n- `t: number`: Stepping: 0 → 1 through the step; -1 planted.\n- `readonly from: Vec3`\n- `readonly to: Vec3`\n\n### interface FootGoal\n\nFoot-placement IK: say where a foot should be, get the hip/knee/ankle rotations.\n\nAuthors write the body (pelvis height, lean, arms...) and then pin the feet:\n\n  placeFeet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Torso: [20, 0, 0] }, rig, {\n    R: { z: 0.15 },                             // right foot flat, 15 cm ahead\n    L: { z: -0.2, pitch: 30, pivot: 'ball' },   // left heel raised on its toes\n  })\n\nCoordinates are the character's ground frame: y up from the floor, z forward. The solve\nis planar (legs bend about X, knees forward); lateral offsets are ignored. It accounts\nfor the root's position, rotation and squash, so a squashed or leaning body still\nkeeps its feet exactly where they were asked…\n\n- `z: number`: Forward position of the ankle (m) when the foot is flat.\n- `x?: number`: Sideways position (m, + = the character's left). Default: under the hip at rest. Only matters when the root is turned (e.g. a pivot on one foot); the solve itself stays in the leg's plane.\n- `y?: number`: Height of the sole above the floor (m). 0 = standing on it.\n- `pitch?: number`: Sole pitch in degrees: + = toes down / heel raised, − = toes up.\n- `pivot?: 'heel' | 'ball' | 'ankle'`: Point that stays at (z, y) while pitching: heel (heel strike), toe tip (tiptoe, toe-off) or ankle.\n- `follow?: number`: 0..1: let the foot hang from the shin instead of holding its world pitch (swinging feet, dangling in the air). 1 = foot at `relax` degrees relative to the shin.\n- `relax?: number`: Foot angle relative to the shin when following (default 15 = toes slightly down).\n\n### gaitClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction gaitClip(rig: RigSpec, g: GaitSpec): ClipDef\n```\n\n### gaitPartners()\n### class SpringChain\n\nA chain of points hanging off a moving root. Call `update(dt, root, basis)` every frame\nwith the root's world position and its orientation (three columns: right, up, forward),\nthen read `points` (root first).\n\n- `new SpringChain(o: SpringChainOptions)`\n- `readonly points: Vec3[]`\n- `o: Required<SpringChainOptions>`\n- `reset(root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`: Put the chain straight out in its rest pose (no swing).\n- `update(dt: number, root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`\n- `swing(basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): number`: How far the tip is from where the rest pose puts it (m): how much it is swinging.\n\n### interface SpringChainOptions\n\n- `segments: number`: Points after the root (≥ 1).\n- `length: number`: Length of each segment (m).\n- `rest?: Vec3`: Rest direction from the root in the root's own space (normalised; default straight back, −Z).\n- `stiffness?: number`: Pull toward the rest pose per second (0 floppy … 30 stiff). Default 10.\n- `keep?: number`: Velocity kept per 1/60 s (0..1). Default 0.94.\n- `gravity?: number`: Gravity on the chain (m/s²). Default 6 (lighter than real: tails hold up a bit).\n\n### class Squash\n\nSquash and stretch as a damped spring on `value` (0 = rest, + stretched, − squashed).\n`scale()` turns it into a volume-preserving pair: `const [h, v] = squash.scale();\nmesh.scale.set(h, v, h)`.\n\n- `value: number`\n- `velocity: number`\n- `stiffness: number`: Spring stiffness and damping (a critically damped spring has damping = 2√stiffness).\n- `damping: number`\n- `amount: number`: 0 turns it off; 2.5 is rubbery.\n- `kick(v: number): void`: Add a kick: negative squashes (a landing), positive stretches (a jump).\n- `set(v: number): void`: Set the shape directly (a held squash).\n- `update(dt: number): void`\n- `scale(out: [number, number] = [1, 1]): [number, number]`: [horizontal, vertical] scale: y = 1 + s, xz = 1 / √(1 + s), so the volume stays put.\n\n### twoBoneIK()\n\n```ts\nfunction twoBoneIK(root: Vec3, target: Vec3, a: number, b: number, pole: Vec3, out: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0]): Vec3\n```\n\nWhere the middle joint of a two-bone limb goes (a knee, an elbow) so the end reaches\n`target` from `root` with bones `a` and `b` long, bending toward `pole` (a point the knee\npoints at). Analytic (the law of cosines), no iterations; a target out of reach straightens\nthe limb toward it, one too close folds it as far as it goes. Returns the joint, into `out`.\n\n### validateClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction validateClip(clip: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec): string[]\n```\n\nProblems with a clip definition itself (unknown joints, bad key order, loop mismatch).\n### applySky()\n\n```ts\nfunction applySky(engine: Pick<Engine, 'sun' | 'ambient' | 'scene' | 'setSunDirection'>, s: SkyState): void\n```\n\nPut a sky on the engine: sun direction, colour and strength, ambient light, background.\n\n### bayer4()\n\n```ts\nfunction bayer4(): any\n```\n\nA 4 x 4 ordered dither threshold per art pixel (0..1): keep a pixel where it is below its opacity.\n### class Boids\n\n- `new Boids(count: number, o: BoidOptions = {})`\n- `readonly count: number`\n- `readonly pos: Float32Array`\n- `readonly vel: Float32Array`\n- `o: Required<Omit<BoidOptions, 'bounds' | 'seed'>> & { bounds: BoidOptions['bounds'] }`\n- `seek: Vec3 | null`: A point everyone is drawn toward (null: none).\n- `seekWeight: number`\n- `flee: { at: Vec3; radius: number } | null`: A threat to scatter from.\n- `fleeWeight: number`\n- `obstacles: { x: number; y: number; z: number; r: number }[]`: Spheres to steer around (x, y, z, r).\n- `spacing(): number`: Average distance to the nearest neighbour (tests, tools).\n- `order(): { speed: number; alignment: number }`: Average speed and how lined up the headings are (0 random, 1 all the same way).\n- `step(dt: number): void`\n\n### interface Branch\n\n- `from: V3`\n### class Decals\n\n- `new Decals(scene: Scene, o: { capacity?: number } = {})`\n- `readonly meshes: Map<\"ring\" | \"crack\" | \"footprint\" | \"scorch\" | \"splat\", InstancedMesh<BufferGeometry<NormalBufferAttributes, BufferGeometryEventMap>, Material<...> | Material…`\n- `readonly o: { capacity?: number }`\n- `add(shape: DecalShape, at: Vector3Like, normal: Vector3Like, o: DecalOptions = {}): number`: Lay a mark at `at` on a surface facing `normal`. Returns its index in that shape's pool.\n- `count(shape?: DecalShape): number`: Marks alive (per shape or all).\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Per frame: age the marks; old ones dither away over a second.\n- `clear(): void`: Remove every mark (the meshes stay for reuse).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### type DecalShape\n\n```ts\ntype DecalShape = (typeof DECAL_SHAPES)[number]\n```\n\n### decodeState()\n\n```ts\nfunction decodeState(v: unknown): unknown\n```\n\n`encodeState` undone: a deep copy with the marked numbers (and the game's own `@` strings) back.\n\n### drawSheet()\n### groundFog()\n\n```ts\nfunction groundFog(o: { color?: number; top?: number; amount?: number; near?: number; far?: number } = {}): { node: Node; color: UniformNode<\"color\", Color>; amount: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; top: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; }\n```\n\nFog for `scene.fogNode` with live settings (uniforms: changing them never recompiles):\nground mist that thickens below `top` (m) and a haze that grows with distance from the\ncamera, both up to `amount` (0..1), in `color` (match the sky).\n\n  const mist = groundFog({ color: s.sky, top: 1.5 });\n  (scene as { fogNode: unknown }).fogNode = mist.node;\n  mist.amount.value = 0.8; mist.color.value.setHex(s.sky);\n### class Mirror\n\n- `new Mirror(o: MirrorOptions = {})`\n- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n- `enabled: boolean`: False: the glass shows plain glass and nothing is rendered for it.\n- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene, camera: Camera, width: number, height: number): boolean`: Reflect `camera` in the glass and draw `scene` from there into the texture (sized `width` x `height`, the art resolution). Skipped when the camera is behind the glass.\n- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`), from its camera, at its art size. Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs (nothing is drawn).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface MirrorOptions\n\n- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Width and height of the glass (m). Default [4, 2].\n- `tint?: number`: A colour the reflection leans toward, and how much (0..1). Default a faint blue, 0.15.\n- `tintAmount?: number`\n\n### class NavGrid\n\n- `new NavGrid(width: number, height: number, o: NavGridOptions = {})`\n- `static fromRows(rows: readonly string[], o: NavGridOptions & { blocked?: string } = {}): NavGrid`: From an ASCII map: `blocked` characters are closed, everything else open. Default '# ': walls and pits (a ' ' has no floor in RoomKit's maps); past the end of a short row is a wall.\n- `readonly width: number`\n- `readonly height: number`\n- `readonly cell: number`\n- `readonly ox: number`: World x, z of cell (0, 0)'s corner.\n- `readonly oz: number`\n- `readonly open: Uint8Array`: 1 = walkable.\n- `version: number`: Bumped by `setOpen`: flow fields rebuild.\n- `flowBuilds: number`: How many times a flow field was built (tools: should be one per target cell change).\n- `col(x: number): number`\n- `row(z: number): number`\n- `centerX(col: number): number`: World x, z of a cell's centre.\n- `centerZ(row: number): number`\n- `isOpen(col: number, row: number): boolean`\n- `walkable(x: number, z: number): boolean`: Is the world point on a walkable cell?\n- `setOpen(col: number, row: number, open: boolean): void`\n- `path(from: readonly [number, number, number], to: readonly [number, number, number]): [number, number, number][] | null`: Shortest path between two world points (x, z used; y kept from `from`): A* over cells, no corner cutting, then smoothed so it only turns where a wall is in the way. Null when there is no way. The first point is `from`, the last `to` (s\n- `smooth(pts: [number, number, number][]): [number, number, number][]`: Drop every point the path can skip in a straight line.\n- `lineOfSight(ax: number, az: number, bx: number, bz: number, radius = 0): boolean`: Can you see (or walk straight) from a to b? Walks the cells under the segment (a DDA); `radius` > 0 also tests two lines offset sideways (a body that wide fits).\n- `castWall(ax: number, az: number, dx: number, dz: number, max: number): number`: Distance from a along a direction to the first closed cell (at most `max`): the same cell walk as `lineOfSight`, so a vision cone drawn with it shows exactly what a guard can see.\n- `flowTo(x: number, z: number): boolean`: A flow field toward the world point (x, z): the walking distance from every cell to it. Rebuilt only when the target changes cell or the grid changed (`version`). Returns whether it was rebuilt.\n- `flowDistance(x: number, z: number): number`: Walking distance to the flow target from a world point (Infinity: no way).\n- `flowDirection(x: number, z: number, out: [number, number]): boolean`: Which way to go from (x, z) toward the flow target: the unit direction to the lowest-distance neighbour (into `out` [x, z]). Returns false at the target or with no way.\n\n### interface NavGridOptions\n\nNavigation on a grid: which cells can be walked, the shortest path between two points\n(A*, 8-connected, no corner cutting, smoothed by line of sight), a flow field toward one\ntarget (one Dijkstra fill, then any number of agents read a direction per cell for free),\nand line-of-sight tests (vision cones, stealth). Pure and allocation-light; unit-tested.\n\n  const nav = NavGrid.fromRows(['#########', '#...#...#', '#.#...#.#', '#########'], { cell: 1, origin: [-4.5, 0, -2] });\n  const path = nav.path([-3, 0, -1], [3, 0, -1]);       // world points, corners only\n  nav.flowTo(hero.x, hero.z);                            // once when the target changes cell\n  nav.flowDirection(x, z, out);…\n\n- `cell?: number`: Metres per cell. Default 1.\n- `origin?: readonly [number, number, number]`: World x, z of the top-left cell's corner (column 0, row 0). Default: centred on the origin.\n\n### interface Noise\n\n- `readonly seed: number`\n### class Precipitation\n\n- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n- `get intensity: number`: Share of the drops falling (0..1).\n- `get speed: number`: Fall speed (m/s).\n- `update(dt: number, center: Vector3): void`: Per frame (game time): advance the fall and follow `center`.\n- `splashes(dt: number): number`: How many drops hit the ground in `dt` seconds at this intensity (for splash particles, ripples).\n- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n\n### type PrecipitationKind\n\n```ts\ntype PrecipitationKind = 'rain' | 'snow'\n```\n\n### interface PrecipitationOptions\n\n- `kind: PrecipitationKind`\n- `count: number`: Most drops at once (the instance count).\n- `area?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Width, height and depth of the air the drops fall through, around the centre.\n- `color?: number`: Drop colour (hex).\n- `speed?: number`: Fall speed (m/s). Rain 16, snow 1.4.\n\n### interface Recording\n\n- `readonly format: 1`\n- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that recorded it (a different one may not replay the same).\n- `readonly game: string`: The game's name when it was recorded.\n### class RenderView\n\n- `new RenderView(o: RenderViewOptions = {})`\n- `static screen(object: Object3D): void`: Put `object` (and its children) on the screens' layer.\n- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n- `every: number`: Render every nth frame.\n- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n- `enabled: boolean`\n- `get texture: Texture`\n- `setSize(w: number, h: number): void`: Resize the texture (the camera's aspect follows).\n- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene): boolean`: Draw `scene` from the view's camera into its texture, if this is one of its frames. True if it drew.\n- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`). Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs.\n- `screenMaterial(): MeshBasicNodeMaterial`: An unlit material showing the view (a new one each call: tint it as you like).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface RenderViewOptions\n\n- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Texture size in pixels (default [160, 90]).\n- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view, degrees (default 60).\n- `near?: number`\n- `far?: number`\n- `every?: number`: Render every nth frame (default 1): a slow refresh costs less.\n\n### class Rng\n\nSeeded randomness. Everything random in a game comes from an `Rng`, so the same seed always\ngives the same result (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1). Each level gets one, `ctx.random`,\nseeded from the engine's seed and the game's name; fork it by purpose so streams stay\nindependent of how many numbers each one drew:\n\n  const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\n  const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\n\nNever use Math.random in game or engine code (the lint refuses it).\n\n- `new Rng(seed: number | string)`\n- `get state: number`: The generator's whole state: save it, and set it back to draw the same numbers again.\n- `next(): number`: Uniform in [0, 1). mulberry32.\n- `fork(purpose: string | number): Rng`: A child generator for one purpose; does not advance this one.\n- `range(min: number, max: number): number`: Float in [min, max).\n- `int(min: number, max: number): number`: Integer in [min, max] (inclusive).\n- `chance(p: number): boolean`\n- `pick(items: readonly T[]): T`\n### skyAt()\n\n```ts\nfunction skyAt(hour: number): SkyState\n```\n\nThe sky at `hour` (wraps around 24).\n\n### interface SkyState\n\n- `readonly sunDir: [number, number, number]`: Unit vector toward the sun (or the moon, at night).\n- `readonly sunColor: number`\n- `readonly sunIntensity: number`\n- `readonly ambientColor: number`\n- `readonly ambientIntensity: number`\n- `readonly sky: number`: Background (sky) and fog colour.\n- `readonly night: number`: 0 by day, 1 deep at night: lanterns, stars, windows.\n\n### interface Snapshot\n\n- `readonly format: 1`\n- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that took it (a different one may not restore the same).\n- `readonly game: string`: The game's name: a snapshot restores into the same game.\n- `readonly seed: number`: The engine seed and game time when it was taken.\n- `readonly time: number`\n- `readonly clock: ClockState`\n- `readonly random: number`: `ctx.random`'s state.\n- `readonly physics: PhysicsState`\n### swayObject()\n\n```ts\nfunction swayObject(root: Object3D, wind: WindUniforms, o: SwayOptions): void\n```\n\nMake every mesh under `root` sway (its materials replaced by swaying copies).\n\n### interface SwayOptions\n\n- `height: number`: Height (in the mesh's own units) of its top: the lean is 0 at `base` and full there.\n- `base?: number`: Where the lean starts (the trunk below stays still). Default 0.\n- `amount?: number`: Lean at the top per unit of wind. Default 0.15.\n- `phase?: number`: Its own phase (radians): neighbours don't move in lockstep.\n\n### type Team\n\n```ts\ntype Team = 'enemy' | 'player'\n```\n\n### class Timeline\n\n- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n- `readonly duration: number`\n- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n- `playing: boolean`\n- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n- `play(): void`\n- `pause(): void`\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and out). A `cut` key starts a new shot. Null witho…\n- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n\n### interface TimelineLine\n\n- `at: number`\n- `until: number`\n- `text: string`\n- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n\n### interface TimelineOptions\n\n- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n\n### interface TraceRow\n\n- `name: string`\n- `kind: string`\n- `depth: number`\n- `status: Status | null`: This tick's answer, or null if this tick never reached the node.\n### class Tweens\n\nA set of running tweens (the engine keeps one per game: `ctx.tweens`).\n\n- `get count: number`: Tweens still running.\n- `to(target: T, to: Partial<Record<keyof T, number>>, options: TweenOptions = {}): Tween`: Glide `target`'s numeric properties to `to`. A new tween on the same target and property takes over (the old one stops where it is).\n- `value(from: number, to: number, options: TweenOptions, apply: (v: number) => void): Tween`: Tween a plain number from `from` to `to`, calling `apply(v)` every frame.\n- `call(seconds: number, fn: () => void): Tween`: Call `fn` after `seconds` of game time.\n- `cancel(target?: object): void`: Stop every tween on `target` (or everything).\n- `clear(): void`: Stop everything (level unload). Pending `done` promises resolve.\n- `update(dt: number): void`\n\n### interface View\n\n- `readonly container: HTMLElement | null`: The page element the canvas sits in; null headless.\n- `readonly backend: BackendName`\n- `readonly gpuErrors: readonly GpuErrorRecord[]`\n- `readonly recoveries: number`: How many times a lost GPU device was recovered from (0 headless).\n### class WaterSurface\n\n- `new WaterSurface(o: WaterOptions)`\n- `readonly size: readonly [number, number]`\n- `waves: Wave[]`\n- `readonly ripples: RippleField | null`\n- `readonly uOpacity: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n- `readonly uFoamAt: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n- `setWaves(waves: readonly Wave[]): void`: Change the waves (up to MAX_WAVES; the CPU height follows too).\n- `update(time: number, sun?: Vector3): void`: Per frame: the waves' clock (use physics time: floaters read the same), the ripples, the sun.\n- `heightAt(x: number, z: number, t = this.time): number`: World height of the drawn surface at (x, z) (waves and ripples), at the last `update` time or `t`.\n- `covers(x: number, z: number): boolean`: Is (x, z) over this water?\n- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n\n### class Wfc\n\n- `new Wfc(tiles: readonly WfcTile[], width: number, height: number, o: WfcOptions = {})`\n- `readonly tiles: readonly WfcTile[]`\n- `readonly wave: Uint8Array`: Options still open per cell: `wave[cell * tiles + t]` is 1 while tile t is possible.\n- `readonly options: Uint16Array`: How many options each cell has left.\n- `readonly result: Int32Array`: The chosen tile per cell (−1 until it has one option left).\n- `attempt: number`: Starts so far (1 + the contradictions met).\n- `done: boolean`: True once every cell has one tile, false while solving or after giving up.\n- `failed: boolean`\n- `choices: number`: Cells collapsed by choice (the rest followed from propagation).\n- `readonly width: number`\n- `readonly height: number`\n- `restart(): void`: Start again from scratch (each start after the first uses the next seed).\n- `run(): boolean`: Solve to the end (restarting on contradictions). True if every cell has a tile.\n- `step(): boolean`: One collapse: the cell with the least entropy gets one tile, and that is propagated. Returns false when there is nothing left to do (solved, or given up).\n- `entropy(c: number): number`: Shannon entropy of a cell's options, by weight (0 when it has one left).\n\n### interface WfcOptions\n\n- `seed?: number`\n- `border?: string`: The socket every edge on the grid's outside must be (a closed map: '###'). Default: any.\n- `fixed?: Readonly<Record<number, number>>`: Cells set before solving: cell index (x + y × width) → tile index (they may break the border: a way in).\n- `attempts?: number`: Starts allowed before giving up on contradictions (default 30).\n\n### interface WfcTile\n\n- `readonly name: string`\n- `readonly edges: readonly [string, string, string, string]`: North (−z, up the map), east (+x), south (+z), west (−x).\n- `readonly weight?: number`: How often it is chosen, relative to the others (default 1).\n\n### class WindUniforms\n\n- `readonly time: any`\n- `readonly wind: any`\n- `update(time: number, wind: Vector2 | readonly [number, number]): void`: Per frame (game time); `wind` along x and z (its length is the strength).\n\n### woodMaterial()\n\n```ts\nfunction woodMaterial(o: ShaderOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\n```\n\nWood: rings round the y axis, wobbled by noise, light and dark grain, toon-lit.\n","numLines":616,"startLine":1,"totalLines":616}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018sazvor23EMr3ePgSa8ikH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
