{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MBdUFJ6JLEAuuApKXeoBQL","type":"tool_result","content":"# The library (Pixel Engine 0.46.0)\n\nEvery built-in model (`MODEL_LIBRARY`, 151) and texture (`TEXTURE_LIBRARY`, 126) by family, then every imported pack (575 models, 264 textures in `packs/`), generated from the defs. A model's variants (`rock-large-a` … `-f`) share a row. Se\n\n- **Find:** grep this file, filter `library.json` (one record per asset: id, kind, family, pack, tags, size, licence), or search in code: `MODEL_LIBRARY.search('wooden chair')`, `TEXTURE_LIBRARY.search('stone floor')` (ranked: id words, the\n- **Place:** `buildModel(id, { params, palette })`, or `use` it inside your own models; textures with `textureMap(id)`, `spriteSheet(id)`, `hudSprite(id)`. Look at it first: `node check.mjs --sheets <id>` (ASSETS.md).\n- **Packs** are someone else's work, imported into this format and palette: each section says how to load it, and CREDITS.md what its licence asks. Its rows leave out the pack's name and tags, which library.json keeps.\n\n## Models\n\n### architecture (19)\n\n| id | size (m, w × h × d) | params: default (min–max) | palette slots | tags | about |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `door` | 1.48 × 2.2 × 0.32 |  | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, wood orange, wood2 red, iron night, brass sand | architecture, stone, wood | Plank door 2.2 m tall in a stone frame; the leaf is a pivot (`leaf`) hinged on the left, \n| `window` | 2 × 2.26 × 0.42 | width 0.8 (0.4–2), height 1 (0.5–1.8) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, wood orange, wood2 red, glass navy, iron night | architecture, stone, wood | Framed window with a cross mullion, a stone sill and\n| `column` | 0.6 × 2.6 × 0.6 | height 2.6 (1–5) | stone mist, stone2 slate | architecture, stone | Stone column: a square plinth and moulded base, a tapering shaft, a flared capital under a square abacus |\n| `stairs` | 1.2 × 1.08 × 1.8 | steps 6 (2–16)