avour reward ×', default: 1, min: 0, max: 5, step: 0.1 },\n  { id: 'friendMult', label: 'Friendship gain ×', default: 1, min: 0, max: 5, step: 0.1 },\n  { id: 'npcSpeed', label: 'Neighbour walk speed', default: 1.8, min: 0.5, max: 5, step: 0.1 },\n  { id: 'chatRate', label: 'Neighbour chat rate ×', default: 1, min: 0, max: 5, step: 0.1 },\n  { id: 'rainMult', label: 'Rain chance ×', default: 1, min: 0, max: 3, step: 0.1 },\n  { id: 'cheeseVol', label: 'Cheese volatility ×', default: 1, min: 0, max: 3, step: 0.1 },\n  { id: 'textSpeed', label: 'Text speed (chars/s)', default: 35, min: 10, max: 200, step: 5 },\n];\nconst KEY = 'honk:tuning';\nexport const tuning = {};\nexport function resetTuning(id) {\n  for (const t of TUNING) if (!id || t.id === id) tuning[t.id] = t.default;\n  saveTuning();\n}\nexport function setTuning(id, v) {\n  const t = TUNING.find((x) => x.id === id);\n  if (!t) return;\n  tuning[id] = Math.min(t.max, Math.max(t.min, Math.round(v / t.step) * t.step));\n  saveTuning();\n}\nfunction saveTuning() { store.set(KEY, tuning); }\nexport function loadTuning() {\n  for (const t of TUNING) tuning[t.id] = t.default;\n  const s = store.get(KEY);\n  if (s) for (const t of TUNING) if (typeof s[t.id] === 'number') tuning[t.id] = s[t.id];\n}\nfor (const t of TUNING) tuning[t.id] = t.default;\nEOF\ncat > src/core/storage.js <<'EOF'\n// localStorage with a memory fallback, so the game imports and runs in Node and in Hub sessions.\nconst mem = new Map();\nlet ls = null;\ntry { if (typeof localStorage !== 'undefined') ls = localStorage; } catch { ls = null; }\nexport const store = {\n  get(key) {\n    try {\n      const raw = ls ? ls.getItem(key) : mem.get(key);\n      return raw == null ? null : JSON.parse(raw);\n    } catch { return null; }\n  },\n  set(key, value) {\n    const raw = JSON.stringify(value);\n    try { if (ls) ls.setItem(key, raw); else mem.set(key, raw); } catch { mem.set(key, raw); }\n  },\n  remove(key) {\n    try { if (ls) ls.removeItem(key); } catch { /* storage refused: memory still clears */ }\n    mem.delete(key);\n  },\n  has(key) { try { return ls ? ls.getItem(key) != null : mem.has(key); } catch { return false; } },\n};\nEOF\ncat > src/core/rng.js <<'EOF'\n// Pure seeded randomness for day-based world generation: the same seed, day and label always\n// give the same numbers, whatever the frame rate. Presentation uses ctx.random forks instead.\nexport function hash32(s) {\n  let h = 2166136261;\n  for (const ch of String(s)) { h ^= ch.codePointAt(0); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n  return h >>> 0;\n}\nexport class Stream {\n  constructor(seed) { this.s = typeof seed === 'number' ? seed >>> 0 : hash32(seed); }\n  next() {\n    this.s = (this.s + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n    let t = this.s;\n    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n  }\n  range(a, b) { return a + this.next() * (b - a); }\n  int(a, b) { return a + Math.floor(this.next() * (b - a + 1)); }\n  chance(p) { return this.next() < p; }\n  pick(list) { return list[Math.floor(this.next() * list.length)]; }\n  shuffle(list) {\n    const a = list.slice();\n    for (let i = a.length - 1; i > 0; i--) { const j = Math.floor(this.next() * (i + 1)); [a[i], a[j]] = [a[j], a[i]]; }\n    return a;\n  }\n  weighted(entries, weight = (e) => e.weight ?? 1) {\n    let total = 0;\n    for (const e of entries) total += weight(e);\n    let r = this.next() * total;\n    for (const e of entries) { r -= weight(e); if (r <= 0) return e; }\n    return entries[entries.length - 1];\n  }\n}\nexport const dayStream = (world, label, day = world.clock.day) => new Stream(`${world.seed}:${day}:${label}`);\nEOF\ncat > src/core/events.js <<'EOF'\n// A tiny event bus: caught, sold, gift, talked, day… feeds memory, stats and tests.\nexport class Events {\n  constructor() { this.handlers = new Map(); this.log = []; }\n  on(name, fn) {\n    if (!this.handlers.has(name)) this.handlers.set(name, []);\n    this.handlers.get(name).push(fn);\n    return () => { const l = this.handlers.get(name); l.splice(l.indexOf(fn), 1); };\n  }\n  emit(name, data) {\n    this.log.push(name);\n    if (this.log.length > 200) this.log.shift();\n    for (const fn of this.handlers.get(name) ?? []) fn(data);\n  }\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/core/calendar.js <<'EOF'\n// The calendar: four seasons of four days. Pure: tests run it in Node.\nexport const SEASONS = ['spring', 'summer', 'autumn', 'winter'];\nexport const SEASON_NAMES = ['Spring', 'Summer', 'Autumn', 'Winter'];\nexport const DAY_TYPES = ['Market Day', 'Errand Day', 'Show Day', 'Festival Day'];\nexport const YEAR_DAYS = 16;\nexport const FESTIVALS = ['seedToss', 'lanternFloat', 'greatSoup', 'longNight'];\nexport const CONTESTS = [null, 'derby', 'bugOff', 'snowman'];\n\n/** A story day (1…∞) in Village Time: its place in the sixteen-day year. */\nexport function villageDay(day) {\n  const d = ((day - 1) % YEAR_DAYS + YEAR_DAYS) % YEAR_DAYS;\n  const season = Math.floor(d / 4);\n  const type = d % 4;\n  return { calendarDay: d + 1, season, seasonId: SEASONS[season], type, festival: type === 3 ? FESTIVALS[season] : null, contest: type === 1 ? CONTESTS[season] : null, show: type === 2, market: type === 0 };\n}\n\nconst nthWeekday = (year, month, weekday, n) => {\n  const first = new Date(year, month, 1).getDay();\n  return 1 + ((weekday - first + 7) % 7) + (n - 1) * 7;\n};\nconst lastWeekday = (year, month, weekday) => {\n  const last = new Date(year, month + 1, 0);\n  return last.getDate() - ((last.getDay() - weekday + 7) % 7);\n};\n\n/** The calendar on a real date, for the Real Clock. month 0-11. New day at 05:00. */\nexport function realDay(ms) {\n  const dt = new Date(ms - 5 * 3600 * 1000);\n  const m = dt.getMonth();\n  const season = m >= 2 && m <= 4 ? 0 : m >= 5 && m <= 7 ? 1 : m >= 8 && m <= 10 ? 2 : 3;\n  const middle = [3, 6, 9, 0][season];\n  const wd = dt.getDay();\n  const isMiddle = m === middle;\n  const contestDay = nthWeekday(dt.getFullYear(), m, 3, 2);\n  const festDay = lastWeekday(dt.getFullYear(), m, 6);\n  const contest = isMiddle && dt.getDate() === contestDay ? CONTESTS[season] : null;\n  const festival = isMiddle && dt.getDate() === festDay ? FESTIVALS[season] : null;\n  const type = festival ? 3 : wd === 0 ? 0 : wd === 6 ? 2 : 1;\n  return { calendarDay: dt.getDate(), season, seasonId: SEASONS[season], type, festival, contest, show: wd === 6 && !festival, market: wd === 0 };\n}\n\n/** The current calendar for a world: Village Time counts story days, the Real Clock reads the date. */\nexport function calendar(world, realMs = null) {\n  if (world.clock.mode === 'real' && (realMs ?? world.clock.realMs)) return realDay(realMs ?? world.clock.realMs);\n  return villageDay(world.clock.day);\n}\nexport function formatTime(minute) {\n  const h24 = Math.floor(minute / 60) % 24;\n  const m = Math.floor(minute % 60);\n  const h = h24 % 12 === 0 ? 12 : h24 % 12;\n  return `${h}:${String(m).padStart(2, '0')} ${h24 < 12 ? 'AM' : 'PM'}`;\n}\nexport function dateLine(world, realMs = null) {\n  const c = calendar(world, realMs);\n  return `${SEASON_NAMES[c.season]} · ${DAY_TYPES[c.type]} · ${formatTime(world.clock.minute)}`;\n}\nEOF\ncat > src/core/weather.js <<'EOF'\n// Weather: seeded per day with an hourly start and stop. Pure.\nimport { Stream } from './rng.js';\nimport { villageDay } from './calendar.js';\n\nexport const WEATHER_TABLE = [\n  [['sun', 60], ['rain', 30], ['fog', 10]],\n  [['sun', 70], ['rain', 20], ['storm', 10]],\n  [['sun', 50], ['wind', 30], ['rain', 20]],\n  [['snow', 60], ['clear', 40]],\n];\nconst WET = new Set(['rain', 'storm']);\n\n/** The day's weather plan: kind, and the hours it runs. Calm days have a whole-day calm kind. */\nexport function weatherPlan(seed, day, season, rainMult = 1) {\n  const rng = new Stream(`${seed}:weather:${day}`);\n  const table = WEATHER_TABLE[season].map(([kind, w]) => [kind, WET.has(kind) ? w * rainMult : w]);\n  const pick = rng.weighted(table, (e) => e[1]);\n  const kind = pick[0];\n  const calm = season === 3 ? 'clear' : 'sun';\n  if (kind === calm) return { kind, start: 0, stop: 24, calm };\n  const start = rng.int(5, 16);\n  const stop = Math.min(24, start + rng.int(3, 8));\n  return { kind, start, stop, calm };\n}\nexport function weatherAt(plan, hour) {\n  return hour >= plan.start && hour < plan.stop ? plan.kind : plan.calm;\n}\n/** Convenience for a village-day world. */\nexport function weatherForDay(world, day = world.clock.day) {\n  const { season } = villageDay(day);\n  return weatherPlan(world.seed, day, season);\n}\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write tuning, storage, RNG, events, calendar and weather modules"}}}
