{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgksBjRGLbbMo6aPxZffs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The lineup reads well, with the last decorations, Dorrit's soup note and a snowball cap still to go. The About text, exit interview and full test run come next.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1997,"cache_read_input_tokens":917173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1997},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4cb4937-9264-42cc-b44d-b76eca04b6e6","uuid":"f0188c56-5433-4f6a-9a10-eb0203c6a71c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:13:51.458Z","request_id":"req_011CgksBj6AbhA9irgSkjndS","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgksBjRGLbbMo6aPxZffs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AmerexfWCV6TzyLUVJHUWq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef sub(p,a,b):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    if a not in s: print('MISSING',p,a[:60])\n    open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))\nsub('src/data/town.js',\"export const ACRES =\",\"\"\"/** Personal decoration outside each cottage: same shell, different life. */\nexport const COTTAGE_DECO = {\n  dorrit: [['soup-pot', 0.4, 0.8, { scale: 0.34 }], ['soup-pot', 4.6, 0.6, { scale: 0.26 }]],\n  tavi: [['flower', 0.5, 0.5, { params: { species: 1 }, palette: { petal: 'sand' } }], ['flower', 4.5, 0.5, { params: { species: 0 }, palette: { petal: 'sand' } }], ['flower', 0.5, 1.4, { params: { species: 2 }, palette: { petal: 'sand' } }]],\n  nib: [['telescope', 4.4, 0.6, {}]],\n  bartleby: [['kenney-furniture/lounge-chair', 4.4, 0.7, { palette: { wood: 'plum', carpet: 'red', carpetDarker: 'plum' } }]],\n  ottoline: [['cheese-wheel', 0.5, 0.5, { palette: { a: 'plum', b: 'night', c: 'night' } }], ['driftwood', 4.3, 0.8, {}]],\n  rocco: [['tank', 0.6, 0.6, { params: { w: 0.8 }, palette: { water: 'sand', frame: 'orange', sand: 'orange', top: 'orange' }, scale: 0.8 }], ['kenney-furniture/bench-cushion-low', 4.4, 0.7, { palette: { wood: 'night', carpet: 'red', metalLight: 'mist' }, scale: 1.3 }]],\n  ozzie: [['kenney-furniture/cardboard-box-closed', 0.5, 0.6, { palette: { wood: 'sand', woodDark: 'orange' }, scale: 1.4 }], ['kenney-furniture/cardboard-box-closed', 4.4, 0.6, { palette: { wood: 'sand', woodDark: 'orange' }, scale: 1.4 }]],\n  yolanda: [['kenney-furniture/rug-doormat', 2.5, 0.4, { palette: { wood: 'red' }, scale: 2 }], ['kenney-furniture/pillow', 4.4, 0.6, { palette: { carpet: 'orange' }, scale: 2 }]],\n};\nexport const ACRES =\"\"\")\nsub('src/world/town.js',\"\"\"    if (id === 'home-1') {\"\"\",\"\"\"    for (const [m, dx, dz, opts] of COTTAGE_DECO[b.id] ?? []) {\n      const { scale, ...rest } = opts;\n      const def = MODELS.get(m);\n      const palette = rest.palette && def?.palette ? Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(rest.palette).filter(([k]) => k in def.palette)) : rest.palette;\n      const o = this.place(m, [b.x + dx, 0, b.z + b.d + dz], { ...rest, palette, group: obj });\n      o.position.set(dx - b.w / 2, 0, b.d / 2 + dz);\n      if (scale) o.scale.setScalar(scale);\n    }\n    if (id === 'home-1') {\"\"\")\nsub('src/world/town.js',\"import { BUILDINGS, LAMPS, BENCHES, LANDMARKS } from '../data/town.js';\",\"import { BUILDINGS, LAMPS, BENCHES, LANDMARKS, COTTAGE_DECO } from '../data/town.js';\")\nsub('src/systems/story.js',\"\"\"  if (c.season === 3) g.life?.spawnSnowballs?.();\"\"\",\"\"\"  if (villageDay(w.clock.day).calendarDay === 11) once('soupNote', () => sendMail(g, { from: 'dorrit', body: \"Dear {player},\\\\nThe Great Soup is tomorrow, mmhm. Everyone adds three things. Bring something good. Don't bring a boot. Someone always brings a boot.\\\\nDorrit\", arriveDay: w.clock.day }));\n  if (c.season === 3 && Object.values(w.town.objects).filter((o) => o.k === 'snowball').length < 8) g.life?.spawnSnowballs?.();\"\"\")\nEOF\ngrep -rn \"TODO\\|FIXME\\|placeholder\\|stub\" src --include=*.js -il | grep -v pixel-engine | head; grep -rn \"Math.random\" src --include=*.js -l | grep -v pixel-engine | head -5; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='src/data/about.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nTEST=[\n ['How many issues did testing catch?','About 28 that needed a fix: seven crashes or bad data at build and load time, eleven gameplay bugs found by the scripted playthrough and the input monkey, two input bugs found only in the real browser, and eight things I only saw in screenshots.'],\n ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?','Eight. Entering the store, the Aquarium and the Gallery each crashed; a menu-closing press also fired a world action; the Seed Toss froze the player; furniture could trap you at the door; Bartleby slept through his own Day One errand; and Mrs. Gander was missing from the opening scene.'],\n ['What was the most helpful test you ran?','The scripted playthrough on Engine.headless: real input, about 0.4 ms a frame, every milestone from the night bus to Year Two in under a minute. It found most of the gameplay bugs and let me rerun everything after each change.'],\n ['What was the least helpful test you ran?','The 279 warnings from the model checker. A few were useful, but most were about coplanar faces and small floating parts that look fine at game scale, so I mostly stopped reading them and judged from screenshots and the cast line-up.'],\n]\nENG=[\n ['What did you like most about the engine?','Models and clips as plain data, plus Engine.headless. I could write a whole cast of 38 characters from one generator, and run the entire game in Node with the same code that runs on WebGPU.'],\n ['Did you get stuck or guess wrong?','Several small guesses. buildModel throws if a palette names a slot the model lacks, which broke shared furniture palettes. Model params are hard range-checked. I guessed the renderSound signature wrong. The dissolve front is white unless a rim colour is set. And a press shorter than a frame shows in wasPressed but not isDown, which lost taps at low frame rates.'],\n ['What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?','The whole UI layer: a mixed-case bitmap font, a screen stack with focus and hit areas, dialogue with voices, and prompts that follow the last device. Close behind were the generator-based scene runner and the tile world with its own collision.'],\n ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?','Judging what a screen really looks like. Screenshots on the software GPU are slow, the first frames take seconds while pipelines compile, and Mirror and RenderView cannot be exercised headless, so visual bugs surfaced late compared with logic bugs.'],\n ['What did you change in the engine, and why?','None. pixel-engine.js ships byte for byte, and a test asserts it.'],\n ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?','Mixed-case text in the HUD with a retained widget layer for focus and hit areas. Every game with menus has to rebuild that, and it was the largest single piece of work outside the game itself.'],\n]\nPROMPT=[\n ['What did you like most about this prompt?','The plan is concrete and honest about what was verified. The tested recipes, such as the browser flags and the importmap packaging, worked first time and saved hours. The writing samples also set a clear voice to match.'],\n ['What was confusing?','Little. I had to decide how to write the source in the file name, since a colon cannot go in one, so I used AnimalCrossingCityFolk. The plan also asks for a stargazing camera glide that an orthographic ground view cannot show, so I used a full-screen star field instead.'],\n ['What was the hardest thing to do?','Breadth at a consistent quality. Every system ships together, including eight venues, four festivals, three contests, a Hub round and two Visit transports, and each needs its own small joke. Keeping all of it wired together was harder than any single feature.'],\n ['What would you change in this prompt?','I would name the exact file-name form for sources with punctuation, and say which plan details are firm and which are only suggestions. Content floors could also be lower for the cosmetic lists, so more effort goes to feel.'],\n]\nnew=\"\"\"export const FEEDBACK = {\n  testing: %s,\n  engine: %s,\n  prompt: %s,\n};\"\"\" % (json.dumps(TEST,indent=4,ensure_ascii=False),json.dumps(ENG,indent=4,ensure_ascii=False),json.dumps(PROMPT,indent=4,ensure_ascii=False))\ns=re.sub(r\"export const FEEDBACK = \\{.*?\\n\\};\",lambda m:new,s,count=1,flags=re.S)\ns=s.replace(\"testing: 'Headless simulation in Node, a scripted playthrough on Engine.headless, Playwright browser checks on file://, the AI Hub harness, two-page Visit tests, and model sheets, behind one command'\",\"testing: 'One command, node tests/run.mjs: rule checks in Node, a scripted playthrough of the whole game with replay, an attract loop and input monkey on Engine.headless, Playwright browser checks on file:// with stub pad and touch profiles, the AI Hub harness in all four scenarios, two-page Visit tests, and model sheets'\")\ns=s.replace(\"research: 'None beyond the supplied plan, kit docs and Hub README'\",\"research: 'None beyond the supplied plan, the engine kit docs and the Hub README'\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > tools/exit_interview.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Writes ../exit-interview.json from the same text the About screen shows, and checks it parses.\nimport { writeFileSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { SOURCE_INFORMATION, FEEDBACK } from '../src/data/about.js';\nconst answers = (list) => list.map(([, a]) => a);\nconst out = {\n  sourceInformation: SOURCE_INFORMATION,\n  testingFeedback: answers(FEEDBACK.testing),\n  engineFeedback: answers(FEEDBACK.engine),\n  promptFeedback: answers(FEEDBACK.prompt),\n  aiHub: {\n    name: 'Honk If You Owe',\n    tagline: 'A village, a goose, and a very long payment plan',\n    description: 'You step off the last bus at the end of the line and, within ninety seconds, owe a goose 8,000 beans. Catch, dig, grow, gossip and pay it off through a sixteen-day year, one bus ride from the neon Big City.',\n    type: 'Game',\n    genre: 'Life Sim',\n    source: 'Animal Crossing: City Folk',\n    series: 'Animal Crossing',\n    players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Move with stick or WASD; Cross or E to talk and use; Square or Space for tools; Triangle or Tab for Pockets; Options or Esc to pause.',\n    tags: ['pixel art', '3d', 'comedy', 'exploration', 'versus'],\n  },\n};\nconst path = new URL('../../exit-interview.json', import.meta.url);\nwriteFileSync(path, `${JSON.stringify(out, null, 2)}\\n`);\nJSON.parse(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));\nconsole.log('exit-interview.json written');\nEOF\nnode tools/exit_interview.mjs; node tools/build.mjs | tail -1; ls -la .. | cut -c30- ; sed -i 's/^- polish batch done.*/- polish batch done; About feedback + exit interview written (tools\\/exit_interview.mjs from src\\/data\\/about.js). NEXT: final full `node tests\\/run.mjs` (takes ~15 min, run in background), cleanup, final reply with Source Info + feedback./' ../PROGRESS.md","description":"Add decoration, write About feedback and exit interview, rebuild"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1997,"cache_read_input_tokens":917173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1997},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4cb4937-9264-42cc-b44d-b76eca04b6e6","uuid":"579c38ae-24f1-4014-8359-99be30a26dba","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:14:26.247Z","request_id":"req_011CgksBj6AbhA9irgSkjndS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AmerexfWCV6TzyLUVJHUWq":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef sub(p,a,b):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    if a not in s: print('MISSING',p,a[:60])\n    open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))\nsub('src/data/town.js',\"export const ACRES =\",\"\"\"/** Personal decoration outside each cottage: same shell, different life. */\nexport const COTTAGE_DECO = {\n  dorrit: [['soup-pot', 0.4, 0.8, { scale: 0.34 }], ['soup-pot', 4.6, 0.6, { scale: 0.26 }]],\n  tavi: [['flower', 0.5, 0.5, { params: { species: 1 }, palette: { petal: 'sand' } }], ['flower', 4.5, 0.5, { params: { species: 0 }, palette: { petal: 'sand' } }], ['flower', 0.5, 1.4, { params: { species: 2 }, palette: { petal: 'sand' } }]],\n  nib: [['telescope', 4.4, 0.6, {}]],\n  bartleby: [['kenney-furniture/lounge-chair', 4.4, 0.7, { palette: { wood: 'plum', carpet: 'red', carpetDarker: 'plum' } }]],\n  ottoline: [['cheese-wheel', 0.5, 0.5, { palette: { a: 'plum', b: 'night', c: 'night' } }], ['driftwood', 4.3, 0.8, {}]],\n  rocco: [['tank', 0.6, 0.6, { params: { w: 0.8 }, palette: { water: 'sand', frame: 'orange', sand: 'orange', top: 'orange' }, scale: 0.8 }], ['kenney-furniture/bench-cushion-low', 4.4, 0.7, { palette: { wood: 'night', carpet: 'red', metalLight: 'mist' }, scale: 1.3 }]],\n  ozzie: [['kenney-furniture/cardboard-box-closed', 0.5, 0.6, { palette: { wood: 'sand', woodDark: 'orange' }, scale: 1.4 }], ['kenney-furniture/cardboard-box-closed', 4.4, 0.6, { palette: { wood: 'sand', woodDark: 'orange' }, scale: 1.4 }]],\n  yolanda: [['kenney-furniture/rug-doormat', 2.5, 0.4, { palette: { wood: 'red' }, scale: 2 }], ['kenney-furniture/pillow', 4.4, 0.6, { palette: { carpet: 'orange' }, scale: 2 }]],\n};\nexport const ACRES =\"\"\")\nsub('src/world/town.js',\"\"\"    if (id === 'home-1') {\"\"\",\"\"\"    for (const [m, dx, dz, opts] of COTTAGE_DECO[b.id] ?? []) {\n      const { scale, ...rest } = opts;\n      const def = MODELS.get(m);\n      const palette = rest.palette && def?.palette ? Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(rest.palette).filter(([k]) => k in def.palette)) : rest.palette;\n      const o = this.place(m, [b.x + dx, 0, b.z + b.d + dz], { ...rest, palette, group: obj });\n      o.position.set(dx - b.w / 2, 0, b.d / 2 + dz);\n      if (scale) o.scale.setScalar(scale);\n    }\n    if (id === 'home-1') {\"\"\")\nsub('src/world/town.js',\"import { BUILDINGS, LAMPS, BENCHES, LANDMARKS } from '../data/town.js';\",\"import { BUILDINGS, LAMPS, BENCHES, LANDMARKS, COTTAGE_DECO } from '../data/town.js';\")\nsub('src/systems/story.js',\"\"\"  if (c.season === 3) g.life?.spawnSnowballs?.();\"\"\",\"\"\"  if (villageDay(w.clock.day).calendarDay === 11) once('soupNote', () => sendMail(g, { from: 'dorrit', body: \"Dear {player},\\\\nThe Great Soup is tomorrow, mmhm. Everyone adds three things. Bring something good. Don't bring a boot. Someone always brings a boot.\\\\nDorrit\", arriveDay: w.clock.day }));\n  if (c.season === 3 && Object.values(w.town.objects).filter((o) => o.k === 'snowball').length < 8) g.life?.spawnSnowballs?.();\"\"\")\nEOF\ngrep -rn \"TODO\\|FIXME\\|placeholder\\|stub\" src --include=*.js -il | grep -v pixel-engine | head; grep -rn \"Math.random\" src --include=*.js -l | grep -v pixel-engine | head -5; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='src/data/about.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nTEST=[\n ['How many issues did testing catch?','About 28 that needed a fix: seven crashes or bad data at build and load time, eleven gameplay bugs found by the scripted playthrough and the input monkey, two input bugs found only in the real browser, and eight things I only saw in screenshots.'],\n ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?','Eight. Entering the store, the Aquarium and the Gallery each crashed; a menu-closing press also fired a world action; the Seed Toss froze the player; furniture could trap you at the door; Bartleby slept through his own Day One errand; and Mrs. Gander was missing from the opening scene.'],\n ['What was the most helpful test you ran?','The scripted playthrough on Engine.headless: real input, about 0.4 ms a frame, every milestone from the night bus to Year Two in under a minute. It found most of the gameplay bugs and let me rerun everything after each change.'],\n ['What was the least helpful test you ran?','The 279 warnings from the model checker. A few were useful, but most were about coplanar faces and small floating parts that look fine at game scale, so I mostly stopped reading them and judged from screenshots and the cast line-up.'],\n]\nENG=[\n ['What did you like most about the engine?','Models and clips as plain data, plus Engine.headless. I could write a whole cast of 38 characters from one generator, and run the entire game in Node with the same code that runs on WebGPU.'],\n ['Did you get stuck or guess wrong?','Several small guesses. buildModel throws if a palette names a slot the model lacks, which broke shared furniture palettes. Model params are hard range-checked. I guessed the renderSound signature wrong. The dissolve front is white unless a rim colour is set. And a press shorter than a frame shows in wasPressed but not isDown, which lost taps at low frame rates.'],\n ['What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?','The whole UI layer: a mixed-case bitmap font, a screen stack with focus and hit areas, dialogue with voices, and prompts that follow the last device. Close behind were the generator-based scene runner and the tile world with its own collision.'],\n ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?','Judging what a screen really looks like. Screenshots on the software GPU are slow, the first frames take seconds while pipelines compile, and Mirror and RenderView cannot be exercised headless, so visual bugs surfaced late compared with logic bugs.'],\n ['What did you change in the engine, and why?','None. pixel-engine.js ships byte for byte, and a test asserts it.'],\n ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?','Mixed-case text in the HUD with a retained widget layer for focus and hit areas. Every game with menus has to rebuild that, and it was the largest single piece of work outside the game itself.'],\n]\nPROMPT=[\n ['What did you like most about this prompt?','The plan is concrete and honest about what was verified. The tested recipes, such as the browser flags and the importmap packaging, worked first time and saved hours. The writing samples also set a clear voice to match.'],\n ['What was confusing?','Little. I had to decide how to write the source in the file name, since a colon cannot go in one, so I used AnimalCrossingCityFolk. The plan also asks for a stargazing camera glide that an orthographic ground view cannot show, so I used a full-screen star field instead.'],\n ['What was the hardest thing to do?','Breadth at a consistent quality. Every system ships together, including eight venues, four festivals, three contests, a Hub round and two Visit transports, and each needs its own small joke. Keeping all of it wired together was harder than any single feature.'],\n ['What would you change in this prompt?','I would name the exact file-name form for sources with punctuation, and say which plan details are firm and which are only suggestions. Content floors could also be lower for the cosmetic lists, so more effort goes to feel.'],\n]\nnew=\"\"\"export const FEEDBACK = {\n  testing: %s,\n  engine: %s,\n  prompt: %s,\n};\"\"\" % (json.dumps(TEST,indent=4,ensure_ascii=False),json.dumps(ENG,indent=4,ensure_ascii=False),json.dumps(PROMPT,indent=4,ensure_ascii=False))\ns=re.sub(r\"export const FEEDBACK = \\{.*?\\n\\};\",lambda m:new,s,count=1,flags=re.S)\ns=s.replace(\"testing: 'Headless simulation in Node, a scripted playthrough on Engine.headless, Playwright browser checks on file://, the AI Hub harness, two-page Visit tests, and model sheets, behind one command'\",\"testing: 'One command, node tests/run.mjs: rule checks in Node, a scripted playthrough of the whole game with replay, an attract loop and input monkey on Engine.headless, Playwright browser checks on file:// with stub pad and touch profiles, the AI Hub harness in all four scenarios, two-page Visit tests, and model sheets'\")\ns=s.replace(\"research: 'None beyond the supplied plan, kit docs and Hub README'\",\"research: 'None beyond the supplied plan, the engine kit docs and the Hub README'\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > tools/exit_interview.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Writes ../exit-interview.json from the same text the About screen shows, and checks it parses.\nimport { writeFileSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { SOURCE_INFORMATION, FEEDBACK } from '../src/data/about.js';\nconst answers = (list) => list.map(([, a]) => a);\nconst out = {\n  sourceInformation: SOURCE_INFORMATION,\n  testingFeedback: answers(FEEDBACK.testing),\n  engineFeedback: answers(FEEDBACK.engine),\n  promptFeedback: answers(FEEDBACK.prompt),\n  aiHub: {\n    name: 'Honk If You Owe',\n    tagline: 'A village, a goose, and a very long payment plan',\n    description: 'You step off the last bus at the end of the line and, within ninety seconds, owe a goose 8,000 beans. Catch, dig, grow, gossip and pay it off through a sixteen-day year, one bus ride from the neon Big City.',\n    type: 'Game',\n    genre: 'Life Sim',\n    source: 'Animal Crossing: City Folk',\n    series: 'Animal Crossing',\n    players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Move with stick or WASD; Cross or E to talk and use; Square or Space for tools; Triangle or Tab for Pockets; Options or Esc to pause.',\n    tags: ['pixel art', '3d', 'comedy', 'exploration', 'versus'],\n  },\n};\nconst path = new URL('../../exit-interview.json', import.meta.url);\nwriteFileSync(path, `${JSON.stringify(out, null, 2)}\\n`);\nJSON.parse(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));\nconsole.log('exit-interview.json written');\nEOF\nnode tools/exit_interview.mjs; node tools/build.mjs | tail -1; ls -la .. | cut -c30- ; sed -i 's/^- polish batch done.*/- polish batch done; About feedback + exit interview written (tools\\/exit_interview.mjs from src\\/data\\/about.js). NEXT: final full `node tests\\/run.mjs` (takes ~15 min, run in background), cleanup, final reply with Source Info + feedback./' ../PROGRESS.md","description":"Add decoration, write About feedback and exit interview, rebuild"}}}
