{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gs99KgrbQJtc5EHeYHWbkz","type":"tool_result","content":"4875\t- `cells?: readonly [number, number]`: Cells along x and z (default one per metre).\n4876\t- `at?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Where the middle of the grid's height 0 is (default the origin).\n4877\t- `bands?: readonly TerrainBand[]`: Colour by height, lowest first; the last band takes everything above.\n4878\t- `steep?: number`: Faces steeper than this (their normal's y below it) are rock. Default 0.72 (about 44°).\n4879\t- `rock?: number`\n4880\t\n4881\t### class Timeline\n4882\t\n4883\t- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n4884\t- `readonly duration: number`\n4885\t- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n4886\t- `playing: boolean`\n4887\t- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n4888\t- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n4889\t- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n4890\t- `play(): void`\n4891\t- `pause(): void`\n4892\t- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n4893\t- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n4894\t- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n4895\t- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and out). A `cut` key starts a new shot. Null witho…\n4896\t- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n4897\t- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n4898\t\n4899\t### interface TimelineLine\n4900\t\n4901\t- `at: number`\n4902\t- `until: number`\n4903\t- `text: string`\n4904\t- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n4905\t\n4906\t### interface TimelineOptions\n4907\t\n4908\t- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n4909\t- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n4910\t- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n4911\t- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n4912\t- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n4913\t- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n4914\t\n4915\t### interface TraceRow\n4916\t\n4917\t- `name: string`\n4918\t- `kind: string`\n4919\t- `depth: number`\n4920\t- `status: Status | null`: This tick's answer, or null if this tick never reached the node.\n4921\t\n4922\t### class Trail\n4923\t\n4924\t- `new Trail(o: TrailOptions = {})`\n4925\t- `readonly capacity: number`\n4926\t- `width: number`\n4927\t- `life: number`\n4928\t- `readonly head: Color`: Head and tail colours (live: `trail.head.setHex(...)`).\n4929\t- `readonly tail: Color`\n4930\t- `push(p: Vector3, time: number): void`: The trail's newest point (call every frame while it moves).\n4931\t- `reset(): void`: Drop every point.\n4932\t- `get length: number`: Points alive now.\n4933\t- `update(time: number, camera: Camera): void`: Per frame: forget old points, rebuild the ribbon facing `camera`.\n4934\t- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n4935\t\n4936\t### interface TrailOptions\n4937\t\n4938\t- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n4939\t- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n4940\t- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n4941\t- `color?: number`: Head and tail colours (hex).\n4942\t- `tail?: number`\n4943\t- `minStep?: number`: A new point only after moving this far (m). Default 0.05.\n4944\t\n4945\t### TRANSITION_CELLS\n4946\t\n4947\t```ts\n4948\tconst TRANSITION_CELLS: { readonly diamonds: 16; readonly blinds: 12; readonly dissolve: 3; readonly mosaic: 20; }\n4949\t```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4cb4937-9264-42cc-b44d-b76eca04b6e6","uuid":"5bd2f2f6-ed99-4898-a767-8322f6cf84a7","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:34:50.200Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-171818__x10629c/work/HonkIfYouOwe-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-171818/kit/API.md","content":"- `cells?: readonly [number, number]`: Cells along x and z (default one per metre).\n- `at?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Where the middle of the grid's height 0 is (default the origin).\n- `bands?: readonly TerrainBand[]`: Colour by height, lowest first; the last band takes everything above.\n- `steep?: number`: Faces steeper than this (their normal's y below it) are rock. Default 0.72 (about 44°).\n- `rock?: number`\n\n### class Timeline\n\n- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n- `readonly duration: number`\n- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n- `playing: boolean`\n- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n- `play(): void`\n- `pause(): void`\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and out). A `cut` key starts a new shot. Null witho…\n- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n\n### interface TimelineLine\n\n- `at: number`\n- `until: number`\n- `text: string`\n- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n\n### interface TimelineOptions\n\n- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n\n### interface TraceRow\n\n- `name: string`\n- `kind: string`\n- `depth: number`\n- `status: Status | null`: This tick's answer, or null if this tick never reached the node.\n\n### class Trail\n\n- `new Trail(o: TrailOptions = {})`\n- `readonly capacity: number`\n- `width: number`\n- `life: number`\n- `readonly head: Color`: Head and tail colours (live: `trail.head.setHex(...)`).\n- `readonly tail: Color`\n- `push(p: Vector3, time: number): void`: The trail's newest point (call every frame while it moves).\n- `reset(): void`: Drop every point.\n- `get length: number`: Points alive now.\n- `update(time: number, camera: Camera): void`: Per frame: forget old points, rebuild the ribbon facing `camera`.\n- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n\n### interface TrailOptions\n\n- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n- `color?: number`: Head and tail colours (hex).\n- `tail?: number`\n- `minStep?: number`: A new point only after moving this far (m). Default 0.05.\n\n### TRANSITION_CELLS\n\n```ts\nconst TRANSITION_CELLS: { readonly diamonds: 16; readonly blinds: 12; readonly dissolve: 3; readonly mosaic: 20; }\n```","numLines":75,"startLine":4875,"totalLines":5144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Gs99KgrbQJtc5EHeYHWbkz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgktokUPAaSsa8heYuPbg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NKRBfXJsSZkJBStR4jAAgW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-171818__x10629c/work/HonkIfYouOwe-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-171818/src/game.js","offset":275,"limit":70},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10429,"cache_read_input_tokens":41193,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10429},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4cb4937-9264-42cc-b44d-b76eca04b6e6","uuid":"e5a2c1c7-2f52-4618-b329-60b57436a884","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:34:51.787Z","request_id":"req_011CgktokEFrbn2L1Nmc9Jxj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NKRBfXJsSZkJBStR4jAAgW":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-171818__x10629c/work/HonkIfYouOwe-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-171818/src/game.js","offset":275,"limit":70}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NKRBfXJsSZkJBStR4jAAgW","type":"tool_result","content":"275\t      if (c.t === 'now') this.realNow = c.ms;\n276\t      if (c.t === 'loadSave') this.pendingLoad = c.world;\n277\t    }\n278\t  }\n279\t  drawHud(ctx, dt) {\n280\t    const hud = ctx.hud;\n281\t    hud.clear();\n282\t    if (this.mode === 'play' && !this.hideHud) {\n283\t      const idle = this.idleTime > 6 && !this.ui.blocking;\n284\t      this.ui.hudAlpha = idle ? 0 : 1;\n285\t      if (!this.ui.has('placement') && !this.ui.has('credits') && !this.ui.has('stargaze')) {\n286\t        drawWorldHud(this, hud, dt);\n287\t        this.interact.drawPrompts(hud);\n288\t      }\n289\t    }\n290\t    this.life.drawHud(hud);\n291\t    this.festivals.drawHud(hud);\n292\t    this.ui.draw(hud);\n293\t    this.drawReveal?.(hud);\n294\t    this.attract.drawHud(hud);\n295\t    this.overlay.draw(hud);\n296\t    // The pixel cursor\n297\t    const m = this.inp.mouse;\n298\t    if (this.inp.device === 'kbm' && m.seen && m.over) hud.sprite(m.x, m.y, CURSOR, CURSOR_COL, { shadow: false });\n299\t  }\n300\t  // ---- Camera ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n301\t  cameraTarget() {\n302\t    if (this.camFocus) return this.target.set(this.camFocus.x + this.place.ox, this.camFocus.y, this.camFocus.z + this.place.oz);\n303\t    const p = this.player;\n304\t    return this.target.set(p.x + this.place.ox, p.y + 0.9, p.z + this.place.oz);\n305\t  }\n306\t  camTeleport() { this.ctx.camera.teleport(this.cameraTarget()); }\n307\t  updateCamera(dt) {\n308\t    const c = this.camState;\n309\t    if (this.fixedCam) return;\n310\t    const rate = 1 - Math.exp(-dt * 9);\n311\t    c.yaw += (c.yawT - c.yaw) * rate;\n312\t    if (Math.abs(c.yaw - c.yawT) < 0.05) c.yaw = c.yawT;\n313\t    const baseZoom = this.place?.kind === 'room' ? (this.place.camZoom ?? 1.8) : tuning.cameraZoom;\n314\t    const talking = this.ui.has('dialogue');\n315\t    let zoomT = (c.zoomOverride ?? baseZoom) * (talking ? 1.25 : 1);\n316\t    if (this.mode === 'title') zoomT = c.zoomOverride ?? 1.15;\n317\t    if (this.mode === 'attract') zoomT = c.zoomOverride ?? 1.6;\n318\t    c.zoomT = zoomT;\n319\t    c.zoom += (c.zoomT - c.zoom) * (1 - Math.exp(-dt * 5));\n320\t    if (Math.abs(c.zoom - c.zoomT) < 0.002) c.zoom = c.zoomT;\n321\t    const key = `${c.yaw.toFixed(2)}:${c.zoom.toFixed(3)}`;\n322\t    if (key !== c.applied) {\n323\t      c.applied = key;\n324\t      this.engine.setCamera({ preset: 'iso', yaw: c.yaw, pitch: 35, zoom: c.zoom, minZoom: c.zoom, maxZoom: c.zoom }, { syncUrl: false });\n325\t    }\n326\t  }\n327\t  turnCamera(dir) {\n328\t    if (this.place?.kind === 'room') { this.sound('uiError'); return; }\n329\t    this.camState.yawT += dir * 90;\n330\t    this.sound('camera');\n331\t  }\n332\t  zoomStep(dir) {\n333\t    const c = this.camState;\n334\t    const cur = c.zoomOverride ?? tuning.cameraZoom;\n335\t    c.zoomOverride = Math.max(1.2, Math.min(2.4, cur + dir * 0.2));\n336\t  }\n337\t  // ---- Season --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n338\t  refreshSeason(force = false) {\n339\t    const c = this.cal;\n340\t    const changed = force || c.season !== this.season || c.calendarDay !== this.calendarDay;\n341\t    this.season = c.season;\n342\t    this.calendarDay = c.calendarDay;\n343\t    if (changed) this.town.setSeason(c.season, c.calendarDay);\n344\t    this.sky.setSeason(c.season);"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4cb4937-9264-42cc-b44d-b76eca04b6e6","uuid":"13623bd9-03b0-41d5-98de-f94ead257ad1","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:34:51.797Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-171818__x10629c/work/HonkIfYouOwe-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-171818/src/game.js","content":"      if (c.t === 'now') this.realNow = c.ms;\n      if (c.t === 'loadSave') this.pendingLoad = c.world;\n    }\n  }\n  drawHud(ctx, dt) {\n    const hud = ctx.hud;\n    hud.clear();\n    if (this.mode === 'play' && !this.hideHud) {\n      const idle = this.idleTime > 6 && !this.ui.blocking;\n      this.ui.hudAlpha = idle ? 0 : 1;\n      if (!this.ui.has('placement') && !this.ui.has('credits') && !this.ui.has('stargaze')) {\n        drawWorldHud(this, hud, dt);\n        this.interact.drawPrompts(hud);\n      }\n    }\n    this.life.drawHud(hud);\n    this.festivals.drawHud(hud);\n    this.ui.draw(hud);\n    this.drawReveal?.(hud);\n    this.attract.drawHud(hud);\n    this.overlay.draw(hud);\n    // The pixel cursor\n    const m = this.inp.mouse;\n    if (this.inp.device === 'kbm' && m.seen && m.over) hud.sprite(m.x, m.y, CURSOR, CURSOR_COL, { shadow: false });\n  }\n  // ---- Camera ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  cameraTarget() {\n    if (this.camFocus) return this.target.set(this.camFocus.x + this.place.ox, this.camFocus.y, this.camFocus.z + this.place.oz);\n    const p = this.player;\n    return this.target.set(p.x + this.place.ox, p.y + 0.9, p.z + this.place.oz);\n  }\n  camTeleport() { this.ctx.camera.teleport(this.cameraTarget()); }\n  updateCamera(dt) {\n    const c = this.camState;\n    if (this.fixedCam) return;\n    const rate = 1 - Math.exp(-dt * 9);\n    c.yaw += (c.yawT - c.yaw) * rate;\n    if (Math.abs(c.yaw - c.yawT) < 0.05) c.yaw = c.yawT;\n    const baseZoom = this.place?.kind === 'room' ? (this.place.camZoom ?? 1.8) : tuning.cameraZoom;\n    const talking = this.ui.has('dialogue');\n    let zoomT = (c.zoomOverride ?? baseZoom) * (talking ? 1.25 : 1);\n    if (this.mode === 'title') zoomT = c.zoomOverride ?? 1.15;\n    if (this.mode === 'attract') zoomT = c.zoomOverride ?? 1.6;\n    c.zoomT = zoomT;\n    c.zoom += (c.zoomT - c.zoom) * (1 - Math.exp(-dt * 5));\n    if (Math.abs(c.zoom - c.zoomT) < 0.002) c.zoom = c.zoomT;\n    const key = `${c.yaw.toFixed(2)}:${c.zoom.toFixed(3)}`;\n    if (key !== c.applied) {\n      c.applied = key;\n      this.engine.setCamera({ preset: 'iso', yaw: c.yaw, pitch: 35, zoom: c.zoom, minZoom: c.zoom, maxZoom: c.zoom }, { syncUrl: false });\n    }\n  }\n  turnCamera(dir) {\n    if (this.place?.kind === 'room') { this.sound('uiError'); return; }\n    this.camState.yawT += dir * 90;\n    this.sound('camera');\n  }\n  zoomStep(dir) {\n    const c = this.camState;\n    const cur = c.zoomOverride ?? tuning.cameraZoom;\n    c.zoomOverride = Math.max(1.2, Math.min(2.4, cur + dir * 0.2));\n  }\n  // ---- Season --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  refreshSeason(force = false) {\n    const c = this.cal;\n    const changed = force || c.season !== this.season || c.calendarDay !== this.calendarDay;\n    this.season = c.season;\n    this.calendarDay = c.calendarDay;\n    if (changed) this.town.setSeason(c.season, c.calendarDay);\n    this.sky.setSeason(c.season);","numLines":70,"startLine":275,"totalLines":480}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NKRBfXJsSZkJBStR4jAAgW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
