{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TKfeVPQTtuYeEWmuXTQfKw","type":"tool_result","content":"560\t- `distance?: number`: third: orbit distance at zoom 1.\n561\t- `position?: [number, number, number]`: fixed: camera position and look-at target.\n562\t- `target?: [number, number, number]`\n563\t- `projection?: 'perspective' | 'ortho'`: fixed/free: projection.\n564\t- `stiffness?: number`: Follow smoothing; higher is snappier.\n565\t\n566\t### type CameraPreset\n567\t\n568\t```ts\n569\ttype CameraPreset = 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side' | 'third' | 'first' | 'free' | 'fixed'\n570\t```\n571\t\n572\tCamera presets. A game picks ONE at startup (EngineOptions.camera / `?camera=`). For\n573\treviewing, `engine.setCamera()` swaps presets live without touching the world. `free`\n574\tis an authoring tool: fly around, press Enter to fix the view, and paste the printed\n575\t`fixed` config into your game.\n576\t\n577\t### class CameraRig\n578\t\n579\tBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n580\t\n581\t- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n582\t- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n583\t- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n584\t- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n585\t- `zoom: number`\n586\t- `readonly minZoom: number`\n587\t- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n588\t- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n589\t- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n590\t- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n591\t- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n592\t- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n593\t- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n594\t- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\n595\t- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n596\t- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n597\t- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n598\t- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n599\t- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n600\t- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n601\t- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n602\t- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n603\t\n604\t### interface CameraRigState\n605\t\n606\tWhere a rig is and looks, as data (`engine.snapshot()`): the frame after a restore sees the camera the frame after the snapshot did.\n607\t\n608\t- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n609\t- `readonly focus: readonly number[]`\n610\t- `readonly zoom: number`\n611\t- `readonly aspect: number`\n612\t- `readonly position: readonly number[]`\n613\t- `readonly quaternion: readonly number[]`\n614\t- `readonly shaken: readonly number[]`\n615\t- `readonly own: Readonly<Record<string, number>>`: What a preset keeps of its own (an orbit's yaw, pitch and distance).\n616\t\n617\t### createCameraRig()\n618\t\n619\t```ts\n620\tfunction createCameraRig(config: CameraConfig = {}): CameraRig\n621\t```\n622\t\n623\t### class FirstPersonRig\n624\t\n625\tEyes of the character: mouse look (click to lock the pointer) or Q/E to turn. No zoom.\n626\t\n627\t- `new FirstPersonRig(config: CameraConfig = {})`\n628\t- `readonly preset: \"first\"`\n629\t- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n630\t- `readonly zoomable: false`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n631\t- `readonly hidesTarget: true`: First person hides the player model.\n632\t- `yaw: number`\n633\t- `pitch: number`\n634\t- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3; }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n635\t- `describe(): { yaw: number; pitch: number; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n636\t\n637\t### class FreeRig\n638\t\n639\tAuthoring camera. While flying: WASD move, Q/E down/up, drag (or click to lock) to look,\n640\tShift = fast, wheel = field of view. Press Enter to fix it: the view freezes, the player\n641\tgets control, and `fixedConfig()` returns the config to hard-code (preset 'fixed').\n642\tEnter again unfixes.\n643\t\n644\t- `new FreeRig(preset: 'free' | 'fixed', config: CameraConfig = {})`\n645\t- `readonly preset: 'free' | 'fixed'`\n646\t- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera | OrthographicCamera`\n647\t- `fixed: boolean`\n648\t- `yaw: number`\n649\t- `pitch: number`\n650\t- `onFix: ((config: CameraConfig) => void) | null`\n651\t- `setFixed(fixed: boolean): void`: Freeze (or unfreeze) the view.\n652\t- `fixedConfig(): CameraConfig`\n653\t- `describe(): { fixed: boolean; config: CameraConfig; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n654\t\n655\t### class OrthoRig\n656\t\n657\tOrthographic presets: classic 3/4 isometric, straight top-down, straight side-on.\n658\t\n659\t- `new OrthoRig(preset: 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side', config: CameraConfig = {})`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4cb4937-9264-42cc-b44d-b76eca04b6e6","uuid":"aa6228cc-bb94-4a38-8677-b161e577f19f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:35:34.371Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-171818__x10629c/work/HonkIfYouOwe-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-171818/kit/API.md","content":"- `distance?: number`: third: orbit distance at zoom 1.\n- `position?: [number, number, number]`: fixed: camera position and look-at target.\n- `target?: [number, number, number]`\n- `projection?: 'perspective' | 'ortho'`: fixed/free: projection.\n- `stiffness?: number`: Follow smoothing; higher is snappier.\n\n### type CameraPreset\n\n```ts\ntype CameraPreset = 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side' | 'third' | 'first' | 'free' | 'fixed'\n```\n\nCamera presets. A game picks ONE at startup (EngineOptions.camera / `?camera=`). For\nreviewing, `engine.setCamera()` swaps presets live without touching the world. `free`\nis an authoring tool: fly around, press Enter to fix the view, and paste the printed\n`fixed` config into your game.\n\n### class CameraRig\n\nBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n\n- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n- `zoom: number`\n- `readonly minZoom: number`\n- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\n- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n\n### interface CameraRigState\n\nWhere a rig is and looks, as data (`engine.snapshot()`): the frame after a restore sees the camera the frame after the snapshot did.\n\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly focus: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly zoom: number`\n- `readonly aspect: number`\n- `readonly position: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly quaternion: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly shaken: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly own: Readonly<Record<string, number>>`: What a preset keeps of its own (an orbit's yaw, pitch and distance).\n\n### createCameraRig()\n\n```ts\nfunction createCameraRig(config: CameraConfig = {}): CameraRig\n```\n\n### class FirstPersonRig\n\nEyes of the character: mouse look (click to lock the pointer) or Q/E to turn. No zoom.\n\n- `new FirstPersonRig(config: CameraConfig = {})`\n- `readonly preset: \"first\"`\n- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly zoomable: false`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: true`: First person hides the player model.\n- `yaw: number`\n- `pitch: number`\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3; }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `describe(): { yaw: number; pitch: number; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n\n### class FreeRig\n\nAuthoring camera. While flying: WASD move, Q/E down/up, drag (or click to lock) to look,\nShift = fast, wheel = field of view. Press Enter to fix it: the view freezes, the player\ngets control, and `fixedConfig()` returns the config to hard-code (preset 'fixed').\nEnter again unfixes.\n\n- `new FreeRig(preset: 'free' | 'fixed', config: CameraConfig = {})`\n- `readonly preset: 'free' | 'fixed'`\n- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera | OrthographicCamera`\n- `fixed: boolean`\n- `yaw: number`\n- `pitch: number`\n- `onFix: ((config: CameraConfig) => void) | null`\n- `setFixed(fixed: boolean): void`: Freeze (or unfreeze) the view.\n- `fixedConfig(): CameraConfig`\n- `describe(): { fixed: boolean; config: CameraConfig; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n\n### class OrthoRig\n\nOrthographic presets: classic 3/4 isometric, straight top-down, straight side-on.\n\n- `new OrthoRig(preset: 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side', config: CameraConfig = {})`","numLines":100,"startLine":560,"totalLines":5144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TKfeVPQTtuYeEWmuXTQfKw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
